hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1801","1788 - Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far al-Farra', from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Answer the caller when you are invited. And we do not know this hadith as narrated from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel with this chain. And others besides Yahya ibn Kathir narrated it, from Shu'bah, from Abu Ja'far, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disconnected; and Yahya ibn Kathir connected it."
"1802","Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani from 'Abdullah. 1789 - Abu Kurayb and Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-Shaybani narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn al-'Ayizar, from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which deed is best? He said: Prayer at its appointed time. I said: Then which? He said: Then kindness to parents. I said: Then which? He said: Striving in the path of Allah."
"1803","1790 - And al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Rukhami narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Maslamah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ya'fur narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn al-'Ayizar, from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Abu Ya'fur except Sa'id ibn Maslamah."
"1804","1791 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn al-'Ayizar, from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of al-Shaybani, from al-Walid."
"1805","1792 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn al-'Ayizar, from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani who said: The owner of this house narrated to me, pointing to the house of 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"1806","1793 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn 'Ubaydullah, from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The best deed is prayer at its time and kindness to parents. Thus al-Hasan narrated it, from Abu 'Amr."
"1807","1794 - And Hafs ibn 'Amr al-Rabbali narrated it to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Jarir narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The best deed is prayer at its time and kindness to parents. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Isma'il, from Abu 'Amr, from 'Abdullah, except 'Amr ibn Jarir; and we do not know that Isma'il narrated with a chain from Abu 'Amr, from 'Abdullah, except this hadith."
"1808","1795 - And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Reviling a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."
"1809","Abu Ma'mar from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. 1796 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that a governor prayed and gave salutation to his right and to his left, so 'Abdullah said: How did he pick it up; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salutation to his right and to his left. And this hadith was narrated by more than one but they did not raise it with a chain."
"1810","1797 - Muhammad ibn Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, from 'Abdullah who said: I was screened by the wall of the Ka'bah when two men with much fat in their bellies and little understanding in their hearts; one of them said to his companion: Do you think Allah hears what we say? His companion said: When we raise our voices He hears, and when we lower them He does not hear. The other said to him: If He hears when we raise, then He hears when we lower. He said: So I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and this verse was revealed: And you were not screened lest your hearing and your sight bear witness against you, up to His statement: But you thought that Allah does not know much of what you do. And we only preserve this hadith with this wording from the hadith of Abu Ma'mar, from 'Abdullah."
"1811","1798 - Muhammad ibn Jabir ibn Bujayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Sayf ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to teach them the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. And we do not know it as narrated from the hadith of Abu Ma'mar, from 'Abdullah, except through this channel; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Mujahid except Sayf ibn Sulayman."
"1812","1799 - Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah while around the House there were such-and-such idols, so he began striking them and pointing at them with a staff he had, or a stick, saying: Truth has come and falsehood has vanished."
"1813","1800 - Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, from 'Abdullah who said: The moon split while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bear witness. And we do not know anyone who narrated these two hadiths from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, except Ibn Abi Najih."
"1814","1801 - Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, from Shu'bah, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abu Ma'mar, from 'Abdullah who said: The moon split while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - I think he said: at Mina. Thus al-A'mash narrated it, from Ibrahim, from Abu Ma'mar, from 'Abdullah."
"1815","Zirr ibn Hubaysh from 'Abdullah. 1802 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1816","1803 - And 'Ubayd ibn Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Sufyan, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The world will not pass away until a man from my household rules the Arabs, whose name corresponds to my name. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Thawri with this chain except Yahya ibn Sa'id and Asbat ibn Muhammad."
"1817","1804 - 'Ali ibn al-Mundhir and al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, they said: Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Ja'far al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The world will not pass away until a man from my household rules, whose name corresponds to my name. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Shaybani, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, except Ja'far al-Ahmar; and none from Ja'far except Ishaq ibn Mansur."
"1818","1805 - Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of al-Shaybani, from 'Asim."
"1819","1806 - Muhammad ibn 'Umarah ibn Subayh narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Muslim al-Mula'i narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The world will not pass away until a man from my household rules, whose name corresponds to my name. And this hadith is strange; we do not know it as narrated from Abu al-Jahhaf, from 'Asim, except through this channel; and we do not know that Abu al-Jahhaf narrated with a chain from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, except this hadith."
"1820","1807 - 'Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: 'Uthman ibn Shubrumah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of al-Thawri, from 'Asim. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from 'Uthman ibn Shubrumah except Muhammad ibn Fudayl; and these words were narrated from 'Asim by a group, among them: Fitr, Za'idah, Hammad ibn Salamah, and others."
"1821","1808 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): And he certainly saw him in another descent. He said: He saw Jibril at the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, having six hundred wings. And we do not know anyone who said in it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Hammad; and others besides Yahya narrated it, from Hammad, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, stopped."
"1822","1809 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: 'Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah that they said: O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those of your nation whom you have not seen? He said: Bright white from the traces of ablution. And these words were narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various channels; and we do not know it as narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel; and we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from 'Asim except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"1823","1810 - 'Abd al-Warith ibn 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, in a raised report, he said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever waits for it until its matter is concluded or it is buried has two qirats. And we do not know this hadith as narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel."
"1824","1811 - 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath and al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah narrated to us, they said: Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps you will reach prayer with people who pray it outside its time; if you reach it, pray it at its time which you know, then pray with them, and make your prayer with them voluntary. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, except Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash."
"1825","1812 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah who said: The two companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a mount were 'Ali and Abu Lubabah; when the turn of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, they said: Ride until we walk. And he would say: You are no stronger than me, and I am no less in need of reward than you. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"1826","1813 - Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1827","1814 - And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated it to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And this hadith was narrated by Hammad ibn Salamah and Abu 'Awanah, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah; and others narrate it from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah."
"1828","1815 - 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah who said: Allah looked into the hearts of servants and found the heart of Muhammad the best of hearts; then He looked into the hearts of servants and found the hearts of his companions the best hearts of servants, so He made them supporters of His religion. What the believer sees as good is good with Allah, and what the believers see as ugly is ugly with Allah. And this hadith from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Bakr; and others besides Abu Bakr narrated it, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah."
"1829","1816 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sulayman, meaning al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah who said: The preserved ones among the companions of Muhammad know that Ibn Umm 'Abd is the closest of them to Allah in means. End of the seventeenth and beginning of the eighteenth, and much praise belongs to Allah."
"1830","Continuation of the hadith of Zirr. 1817 - Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shayban, meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, meaning Ibn Hubaysh, from 'Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast three days from the beginning of every month, and I never saw him breaking fast on a Friday ever. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) higher than 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud; and we do not know it as narrated from 'Abdullah with this wording except through this channel with this chain; and Shayban, Qays ibn al-Rabi', and others narrated it from 'Asim; and Shayban added: And I never saw him breaking fast on a Friday ever."
"1831","1818 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the 'Isha prayer, then came out to the mosque while the people were waiting for prayer, and said: None of the people of the religions prays at this hour besides you. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from 'Asim with this chain except Shayban."
"1832","1819 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Hasan and al-Husayn: O Allah, I love them, so love them; and whoever loves them has loved me. And we only heard this hadith from Yusuf, from Abu Bakr."
"1833","1820 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Take suhur, for in suhur there is blessing. And this hadith was narrated by more than one, from 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Bakr, with this chain stopped; and we do not know anyone who raised it with a chain from 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Bakr, except Muhammad ibn Bashshar; and Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated it, from Abu Bakr, raised."
"1834","1821 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated it to us with it, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, raising it similarly."
"1835","1822 - Al-'Abbas ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Al-Walid ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah who said: He forbade prayer after 'Asr until the sun sets, and after Fajr, or after the morning prayer, until the sun rises, and at midday - I think he said: in intense heat."
"1836","1823 - Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was a boy herding sheep for 'Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt, and he mentioned some speech, then said: And he wiped my head and said: You are a taught boy."
"1837","1824 - Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sulayman al-Dabbas narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The woman who buries alive and the buried female infant are in the Fire. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, except Muhammad ibn Aban."
"1838","1825 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a campaign when there was revealed upon him: By those sent forth in succession. So I received it from his mouth while his mouth was still moist with it; then a snake came out and entered a hole, so we followed it. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You were protected from its evil as it was protected from your evil. And this hadith was narrated by more than one, from 'Asim."
"1839","1826 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, that he climbed a tree gathering a tooth-stick from arak, and the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at him and marveled at the thinness of his legs. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are heavier in the balance than Uhud. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"1840","1827 - Ahmad ibn al-Hakam ibn Zibyan narrated to us, he said: Al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Nations were presented to me last night with their followers."
"1841","1828 - Muhammad ibn 'Uqbah al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fatimah guarded her chastity, so Allah forbade her offspring to the Fire. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, except 'Amr ibn Ghiyath; and this 'Amr is a Kufan who was not followed in this hadith. And others besides Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated it, from 'Amr ibn Ghiyath, from 'Asim, from Zirr, disconnected."
"1842","1829 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-'Askari narrated to us, he said: Al-Husayn ibn 'Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah who said: I took seventy surahs from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1843","1830 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-'Askari narrated to us, he said: Al-Husayn ibn 'Ali informed us, from Za'idah, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Recite to me. So I recited to him Surah al-Nisa until I reached: Then how when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you against these as a witness. He said: Then his eyes overflowed, and he said: Whoever loves to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it upon the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd."
"1844","1831 - Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Dahir narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Hour will not come until a man from my household rules, whose name corresponds to my name, filling the earth with equity and justice as it was filled with wrong and injustice. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, except 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Quddus."
"1845","1832 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah."
"1846","1833 - And Ahmad ibn 'Uthman ibn Hakim narrated it to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from 'Abdullah who said: Al-Hasan and al-Husayn would come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, jumping upon him and riding him; when they were forbidden from that, he signaled with his hand to leave them. When he finished prayer he embraced them and said: Whoever loves me, let him love these two. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith with this wording from 'Asim except 'Ali ibn Salih."
"1847","1834 - Al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from 'Asim, I think, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah who said: We were taught istikhara as we were taught a surah of the Qur'an. When one of you intends a matter, let him say: O Allah, I seek good from You by Your knowledge, I seek power from You by Your power, and I ask You of Your vast bounty. You are able and I am not able, You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if this matter which I intend, and he names it, is good in my religion, good for me in my worldly affair, and good for me in the outcome of my affair, then make it easy for me - I think he said: then bless it for me; and if it is evil for me in my religious affair, evil for me in my worldly affair, and evil for me in the outcome - I think he said: of my affair - then turn it away from me, make good easy for me, decree it for me, and make me pleased with it."
"1848","1835 - And al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid narrated it to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. And we do not know this hadith as narrated from the hadith of Zirr, from 'Abdullah, except with this chain."
"1849","1836 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Razin, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from 'Abdullah."
"1850","1837 - And Salm ibn Junadah narrated it to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Razin, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from 'Abdullah who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a campaign when there was revealed: By those sent forth in succession. So I received it from his mouth while his mouth was still moist with it. And Ibn Abi 'Ubaydah added, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Razin, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from 'Abdullah who said: And I took seventy surahs from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And we do not know that Abu Razin narrated from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, any raised hadith except this hadith."
"1851","1838 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad Abu Shaybah narrated it to us with it, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi 'Ubaydah narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Razin, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah."
"1852","1839 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from 'Isa al-Asadi, who is 'Isa ibn 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Omens are part of polytheism; and there is none of us except that Allah, blessed and exalted, removes it through trust. And we do not know this hadith as narrated from 'Abdullah except through this channel with this chain."
"1853","1840 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abu Shaybah Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr narrated to us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he was asked which sin is greatest? He said: That you set up a rival to Allah while He created you. He said: Then which? He said: Then that you kill your child fearing he will eat your food. He said: Then which? He said: Then that you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife. And we do not know that 'Abd al-Malik narrated from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, except this hadith."
"1854","1841 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid ibn Ma'dan narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr and Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the morning prayer on Friday Alif-Lam-Mim, the Revelation, and Has There Come Upon Man."
"1855","1842 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, they said: Badal ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid ibn Ma'dan narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il and Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two rak'ahs before Fajr Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One."
"1856","1843 - Al-'Abbas ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Ash'ath narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid ibn Ma'dan narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il and Zirr, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salutation to his right and to his left, meaning in prayer. And we do not know anyone who narrated these hadiths from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il and Zirr, combining them, except 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid."
"1857","1844 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, who said: The first to proclaim their Islam were seven: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Bilal, and he mentioned a group. As for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah protected him through his uncle; as for Abu Bakr, Allah protected him through his people; as for the rest, they were tortured and scorched in the sun. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Za'idah connected except Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr."
"1858","1845 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Asim, from Zirr: And when We turned toward you a group of jinn listening to the Qur'an; when they attended it they said: Listen. He said: Be silent. He said: They were seven, the eldest of whom was Zawba'ah. And some companions of Abu Ahmad raised this hadith to 'Abdullah, and some did not say from 'Abdullah."
"1859","1846 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Mansur, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from 'Abdah, meaning Ibn Abi Lubabah, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a snake or a scorpion has killed a disbeliever, or as though he killed a disbeliever."
"1860","1847 - Ishaq ibn 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Zakariyya narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn 'Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Asbahani narrated to us, from his father, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praise al-Nakha' until I wished my people were from al-Nakha'. And we do not know this hadith with this wording as narrated except from 'Abdullah with this chain."
"1861","1848 - Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Rayhan ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Ar'arah ibn al-Birind narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When there are three, two should not converse privately excluding the third."
"1862","'Amr ibn Maymun from 'Abdullah. 1849 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Abdullah who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), about forty men, and he said: Are you pleased to be a quarter of the people of Paradise? We said: Yes. He said: Are you pleased to be a third of the people of Paradise? We said: Yes. He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, I hope you will be half the people of Paradise; and none enters Paradise except a Muslim soul; and you among the people of polytheism are but like a white hair on the skin of a black bull, and a black hair on the skin of a red bull."
"1863","1850 - And Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"1864","1851 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Abdullah that he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was prostrating with people from Quraysh around him, 'Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt came with the afterbirth of a camel and threw it upon the back of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not raise his head, so Fatimah came, took it from his back, and supplicated against whoever did that. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head he said: O Allah, upon You are the chiefs of Quraysh: Abu Jahl, 'Utbah ibn Rabi'ah, Shaybah ibn Rabi'ah, 'Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt, and Umayyah ibn Khalaf, or Ibn Abi Khalaf - Shu'bah is the doubter. He said: I saw them killed on the day of Badr and thrown into the well, except Umayyah or Ubayy, whose limbs were cut apart so he was not thrown into the pit."
"1865","1852 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: Al-Muthanna ibn Zur'ah Abu Rashid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Al-Ajlah narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, from 'Abdullah who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the mosque with Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, Shaybah and 'Utbah, the two sons of Rabi'ah, 'Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt, and Umayyah ibn Khalaf - Abu Ishaq said: and two other men whose names I do not remember, they were seven in the Hijr - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying; when he prostrated he lengthened prostration, so Abu Jahl said: Which of you will bring the camel of so-and-so and bring us its dung to throw upon Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So the most wretched of them, 'Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt, went and brought it and threw it upon his shoulders while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was prostrating. Ibn Mas'ud said: And I was standing unable to speak, having no clan to protect me, so I was afraid, when I heard Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); she came until she removed that from his shoulder, then faced Quraysh and reviled them, and they did not return anything to her. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head as he used to raise it at the completion of his prostration. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer he said: O Allah, upon You are Quraysh, three times; upon You are 'Utbah, 'Uqbah, Abu Jahl, and Shaybah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left the mosque and met Abu al-Bakhtari, with Abu al-Bakhtari a whip tucked at his waist. When he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he disapproved of his face and said: What is wrong with you? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave me. He said: By Allah I know I will not leave you until you tell me what is wrong with you, for something has befallen you. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew he would not leave him, he informed him and said: Abu Jahl ordered and dung was thrown upon me. Abu al-Bakhtari said: Come to the mosque. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu al-Bakhtari came and entered the mosque. Then Abu al-Bakhtari turned to Abu Jahl and said: O Abu al-Hakam, are you the one who ordered that dung be thrown upon Muhammad? He said: Yes. He said: Then he raised the whip and struck his head with it. He said: Then men rose against one another. He said: And Abu Jahl shouted: Woe to you, it belongs to him; Muhammad only wanted to cast enmity between us and save himself and his companions. And this hadith with this wording, we do not know anyone who narrated it except al-Ajlah; and Isra'il, Shu'bah, Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, and others narrated it, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Abdullah."
"1866","1853 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn Ma'bad narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Abdullah who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was prostrating at the Ka'bah with people from Quraysh around him, then he mentioned similar to the hadith of Shu'bah, adding in it: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head, he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, O Allah, upon You are the chiefs of Quraysh; then he narrated the story. And we do not know anyone who added in this hadith that he said: To proceed, except Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah."
"1867","1854 - 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Isa ibn Sasan and Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, they said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Al-Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The first group to enter Paradise from my nation, their faces like the moon on the night of full moon; and the second group like the best brilliant star in the sky. For each man among them two wives; upon each wife seventy garments, the marrow of their legs seen from behind the garments as red drink is seen in a white glass. And we only preserve this hadith from the hadith of Fudayl, from Abu Ishaq, with this chain."
"1868","1855 - Hamdan ibn 'Ali and Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, they said: 'Ali ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Can none of you recite a third of the Qur'an in a night? They said: O Messenger of Allah, who can bear this? He said: Can none recite Say: He is Allah, the One, for it equals a third of the Qur'an. Thus Sharik narrated it, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Abdullah."
"1869","1856 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Abdullah, who said: 'Utbah ibn Rabi'ah was a friend of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh in pre-Islamic times; when 'Utbah came to Medina he stayed with Sa'd ibn Mu'adh, and when Sa'd came to Makkah he stayed with 'Utbah. 'Utbah used to call him my Yathribi brother. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina, Sa'd ibn Mu'adh came to Makkah as he used to come, and stayed with 'Utbah. He said: I want to circumambulate the House. 'Utbah said to him: Wait until the chiefs of Quraysh disperse from the mosque or from around the House. He said: So he waited a little, then said to him: Go with me. When they came to the House, Abu Jahl met Sa'd and said: O Sa'd, you sheltered Muhammad then circumambulate the House in safety? Sa'd said to him: If you prevent me, I will cut off for you, or I will prevent you from your trade to such-and-such place, a place he mentioned. He said: And their voices rose. 'Utbah said to Sa'd: Do you raise your voice against Abu al-Hakam? He said: Sa'd said to him: And do you say that; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: He will kill you. He said: Then he shook his hand from his hand and said: Muhammad does not lie. He said: So Sa'd circumambulated, then left. 'Utbah's wife came to him and said: Did you not hear what my Yathribi brother said? She said: And what did he say? He said: He claimed that Muhammad will kill me, and Muhammad does not lie. He said: It was only a little until the affair of Badr came. He said: Abu Jahl began going around the people, and he mentioned the hadith in full."
"1870","1857 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with this supplication: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from cowardice and miserliness, evil old age, the trial of the breast, and the punishment of the grave."
"1871","1858 - And I think 'Abdah ibn 'Abdullah narrated it to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated this hadith, from his father, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1872","1859 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubayd ibn 'Aqil narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Hammad Abu 'Attab narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the statement of Allah, blessed and exalted: On the Day the earth is changed to other than earth. He said: A white earth upon which no blood was shed, or upon which no sin was done. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr, from 'Abdullah, raised, except Jarir ibn Ayyub; and Jarir is not strong."
"1873","1860 - Ahmad ibn 'Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun who said: 'Abdullah narrated to us in the treasury house, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying at the House with chiefs of Quraysh sitting, having slaughtered a camel. He said - I think it was Abu Jahl -: Which of you will take this dung with its blood, then wait until Muhammad places his face prostrating and place it upon his back? 'Abdullah said: When the most wretched of them rushed forth and took the dung; when he fell prostrating he placed it upon his back. Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), was informed while a young girl, so she came running and took it from his back. When he finished his prayer he said: O Allah, upon You are Quraysh; O Allah, upon You are Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, Shaybah ibn Rabi'ah, 'Utbah ibn Rabi'ah, and 'Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt, until he counted seven from Quraysh. 'Abdullah said: By the One who sent down the Book upon him, I saw them on the day of Badr in a single well."
"1874","1861 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Abdullah who said: When I killed Abu Jahl I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: This is the Pharaoh of this nation."
"1875","1862 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sunnah ibn Muslim al-Batin, from his father, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, who said: I sat with 'Abdullah for a year and he did not narrate a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then one day he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and his face changed, and he said something like this, or above this, or below this."
"1876","1863 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Utbah, from Muslim al-Batin, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Abdullah, similarly."
"1877","1864 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: 'Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-'Attar narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The righteous dream is glad tidings, being a part of seventy parts of prophethood; and your fire, meaning this one, is a part of seventy parts of the poison of Hell; and as long as a servant waits for prayer, he is in prayer so long as he does not break ablution. Thus Zuhayr narrated it; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Zuhayr except 'Ubayd ibn Ishaq. And 'Amr ibn Thabit narrated it, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr al-Asamm, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly; and others besides 'Amr ibn Thabit narrated it, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr al-Asamm, from 'Abdullah, stopped."
"1878","Al-Rabi' ibn Khuthaym from 'Abdullah. 1865 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from his father, from Mundhir al-Thawri, from al-Rabi' ibn Khuthaym, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew a line for us one day, drew a line to its right, and drew a line to its left, then said: This is the path of Allah. Then he drew lines and said: These are paths; upon each path among them is a devil calling to it. And he recited: And that this is My path, straight, so follow it; and do not follow the paths, lest they separate you. And these words were narrated from 'Abdullah through more than one channel, similar or close to it."
"1879","1866 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Bakrawi 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Mudrik, from Ibrahim, from al-Rabi' ibn Khuthaym, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Say: He is Allah, the One, equals a third of the Qur'an. And this hadith was narrated from Shu'bah by Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh and Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi."
"1880","1867 - Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Abi Diya', from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from al-Rabi' ibn Khuthaym, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A loan twice equals charity once. And we do not know this hadith as narrated from al-Rabi' ibn Khuthaym, from 'Abdullah, except with this chain."
"1881","1868 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from al-Rabi' ibn Khuthaym, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1882","'Amr ibn Salamah from 'Abdullah. 1869 - Ja'far ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Al-Husayn ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Amr ibn Salamah, from 'Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no two Muslims but that between them is a veil from Allah; when one of them says to his companion an insulting word, he tears Allah's veil. And we do not know these words as narrated with this wording from 'Abdullah except 'Amr ibn Salamah."
"1883","Abu al-Ja'd from 'Abdullah. 1870 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from his father, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1884","1871 - And Yahya ibn Habib ibn 'Arabi narrated to us, he said: Al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrate, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from his father, from 'Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is none among you except that a companion from the jinn has been assigned to him. They said: And you? He said: And me, except that Allah helped me against him so he became Muslim. And we only preserve this hadith with this wording from 'Abdullah except with this chain."
"1885","Hubayrah ibn Yarim from 'Abdullah. 1872 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from 'Abdullah who said: Had I known one more knowledgeable of the Book of Allah than me whom a mount could reach, I would have gone to him; I took seventy surahs from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1886","Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid, meaning Sulayman ibn Hayyan, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Abdullah who said: Whoever goes to a soothsayer or a magician and believes him in what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith has been narrated by more than one from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Abdullah. As for the hadith ""I took seventy surahs from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)"", we do not know of anyone narrating it from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, except al-A'mash, and none narrated it from al-A'mash except Abu Usamah and Abdah ibn Sulayman."
"1887","Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Umayr ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Abdullah, in marfu' form, he said: Fasting is a shield, and the changed smell of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk. This hadith has been narrated by others besides Umayr as mawquf."
"1888","Amr ibn Shurahbil from Abdullah: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, and Mansur, and Wasil, from Abu Wa'il, from Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked which sin is greatest. He said: That you set up a rival to Allah while He created you. He said: Then which? He said: Then that you kill your child fearing he will eat your food. He said: Then which? He said: Then that you commit adultery with your neighbour's wife. Then he recited: {And those who do not call upon another god with Allah}. This hadith has been narrated by others besides al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, and not one of them mentioned..."
"1889","Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever deliberately lies about me in order to misguide thereby, let him take his seat in the Fire. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith in musnad form from al-A'mash, from Talhah, except Yunus ibn Bukayr; others besides Yunus narrated it from al-A'mash as mursal."
"1890","Al-Ahnaf ibn Qays from Abdullah: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj. And Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Atiq, from Talq ibn Habib, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Beware, the hair-splitters have perished; beware, the hair-splitters have perished — he said it three times. We do not know of al-Ahnaf narrating from Abdullah except this hadith."
"1891","Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Abdullah: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the adhan of Bilal prevent you from sahur; eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the adhan. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from Abdullah except through this channel with this isnad, though more than one has narrated it from al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi."
"1892","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abdullah, that he looked at some people of al-Zutt and said: These are the most like the jinn of anyone I have seen — meaning the Night of the Jinn. We do not know of this wording being narrated except from Abu Uthman, from Abdullah."
"1893","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abdullah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that he had met a woman, and he mentioned that he had taken a kiss from her or something he mentioned, and it was as if he was asked about its expiation, so Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: {And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours} to the end of the verse."
"1894","Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abu Uthman, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting traders on the way to intercept goods."
"1895","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Samurah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Asim, meaning al-Ahwal, narrated to us, from Abu Uthman, from Abdullah who said: We were commanded that when we see someone announcing a lost item in the mosque, we say to him: May you not find it. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from Abdullah except with this isnad."
"1896","Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Ta'i narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Uthman, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance — or he said: in prayer — he will have nothing to do with Allah, neither lawful nor unlawful. We do not know of these words being narrated with this wording except from Abdullah; more than one has narrated it from Asim, from Abu Uthman, from Abdullah as mawquf, while Abu Awanah narrated it in marfu' form."
"1897","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Duba'i narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Zaynab narrated to us, from Abu Uthman, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I had placed my left hand over my right, so he took my right hand and placed it over my left. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from Abu Uthman, from Abdullah, except al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Zaynab, a Wasiti man from whom Hushaym, Yazid ibn Harun and Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated."
"1898","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Maymun, from Abu Tamimah al-Saluli — Bundar said, and it is also said: al-Salli — from Abu Uthman, from Ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the Isha prayer, then he left and took my hand, and went out to al-Batha, the Batha of Makkah, then he drew a line for him — meaning for Abdullah ibn Mas'ud — then he said: Do not leave your line, and if anyone comes to you, do not speak to him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went where he intended. While I was sitting in my line, some men came to me as if they were al-Zutt, with their hair and bodies, not crossing the line, then going on to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When it was the end of the night, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while I was sitting and said: These have troubled me tonight. Then he entered my line and rested his head on my thigh and slept; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept, he would breathe heavily in sleep. While I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) resting on my thigh, I saw some men as if they were men of the Hijaz, wearing white garments — Allah knows how beautiful they were. A group of them sat at the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and a group at his feet, then they said among themselves: We have never seen anyone given what this Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has been given; his eyes sleep while his heart is awake. Strike a parable for him — I think he said: Of a man who built a palace, then prepared a feast and invited people to his food; whoever answers him eats of his food and drinks of his drink, and whoever does not answer him, he punishes him — or he is punished. Then they ascended, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up. He said: Do you know who they were? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: They are the angels. Do you know what parable they struck? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The parable they struck: the Lord, blessed and exalted, built Paradise and called His servants to it; whoever answers Him enters Paradise, and whoever does not answer Him, He punishes him — or torments him. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from Abdullah except through this channel, though al-Taymi narrated it disagreeing with Ja'far ibn Maymun in its isnad, saying: from Amr al-Bikali, from Abu Uthman."
"1899","Qays ibn Abi Hazim from Abdullah: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us. And Bishr ibn Khalid narrated it to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us — both mentioning that — from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, meaning Ibn Abi Hazim, from Abdullah who said: We remained honoured ever since Umar embraced Islam."
"1900","Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, both saying: Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Isma'il narrated to us, from Qays, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends to take a servant's soul in a land, He gives him some need toward it. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith in marfu' form except Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami."
"1901","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il narrated to us, from Qays, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom Allah has given the Qur'an and he stands with it through the hours of the night and the hours of the day, and a man to whom Allah has given wealth and given him power to spend it in truth. This hadith has been narrated from more than one, and we do not know of it being narrated from Abdullah except through this channel."
"1902","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Abdullah who said: We used to go out in expeditions with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we had no women with us, so some of us asked his permission to castrate themselves — or he said: If only you would permit us, we would castrate ourselves — but he did not permit us; instead he permitted us temporary enjoyment in exchange for a garment."
"1903","Yahya ibn Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abis narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Abdullah who said: A'ishah had a freed slave incumbent upon her from the children of Isma'il, then some captives from Banu al-Anbar arrived, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If it pleases you to fulfil your vow, free someone from these. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from Abdullah except through this channel, and we do not know of anyone narrating it from Isma'il except Ali ibn Abis."
"1904","Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is wrong with me that I do not get angry while the dirt under one of your fingernails and toenails... This hadith: we do not know of anyone narrating it in musnad form from Abdullah except al-Dahhak; others besides al-Dahhak narrate it from Isma'il, from Qays, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as mursal."
"1905","Al-Abbas ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, he said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Abdullah, in marfu' form, he said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three days. This hadith has been narrated from Abdullah through more than one channel."
"1906","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id and Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, both saying: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Isma'il informed us, from Qays, from Abdullah, that he came to Abu Jahl while he still had a spark of life and said: May Allah disgrace you. He replied: Is there a man prouder than one you have killed?"
"1907","Ata ibn Yasar from Abdullah: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Ishaq, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There will be rulers after me who say what they do not do and do what they are not commanded. Whoever strives against them with his hand is a believer, whoever strives against them with his tongue is a believer, and whoever strives against them with his heart is a believer; there is no faith beyond that. We do not know of this hadith being narrated with this wording from Abdullah except with this isnad, and we do not know of Ata ibn Yasar narrating from Abdullah any hadith besides this one, nor do we know that he heard from him though he was early; nor do we know of al-Hasan ibn Amr narrating in musnad form from Mu'awiyah ibn Ishaq except this hadith."
"1908","Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid from Abdullah: Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to recite: {Indeed Allah is the Provider, the Possessor of strength, the Firm}. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, except through the narration of Abu Ishaq from him."
"1909","Abd al-A'la ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rak'ahs at Mina. This hadith has been narrated by more than one from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah."
"1910","And Isma'il ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I heard Idris al-Kufi, meaning al-Awdi, saying: al-A'mash narrated to me, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it. We do not know of anyone narrating it from Idris except Musa ibn A'yan."
"1911","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, that on the Day of Sacrifice he went into the interior of the valley and stoned the Jamrah, the Jamrat al-Aqabah, and said: This is the standing place of the one upon whom Surah al-Baqarah was revealed."
"1912","Ahmad ibn Abdah, Amr ibn Yahya ibn Ghufrah al-Bajali — and the wording is Ahmad's — both said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah who said: The talbiyah of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, You have no partner, here I am; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; You have no partner. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from Abu Ishaq except through the hadith of Aban ibn Taghlib."
"1913","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam and Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah."
"1914","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, that he stoned the Jamrah with seven pebbles, placing the House to his left and Mina to his right, and said: This is the standing place of the one upon whom Surah al-Baqarah was revealed."
"1915","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he prayed two rak'ahs at Mina."
"1916","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he prayed two rak'ahs at Mina."
"1917","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray a prayer outside its proper time except that he combined the two prayers at Muzdalifah, and he prayed Fajr that day outside its usual time. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except Abdullah ibn Mas'ud through the narration of Umarah, from Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah. The meaning of his saying that he prayed Fajr outside its time is that he prayed it earlier than the time at which he used to pray it every day, for he used to pray every day when the dawn had spread, whereas on that day he prayed it when the dawn had just gleamed — so it was before the usual time at which he prayed it every day, not that he prayed it before its obligatory time had entered."
"1918","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Umarah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah who said: I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray a prayer except at its time, except that he combined Maghrib and Isha at Muzdalifah, and he prayed the morning prayer outside its usual time."
"1919","And Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Shortening the sermon and lengthening the prayer is a sign of a man's understanding, so lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermons. Some eloquence is indeed magic. After you there will come people who lengthen sermons and shorten prayers. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from al-A'mash, from Umarah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, except Yahya ibn Adam, from Qays."
"1920","And Muhammad ibn Hisham narrated it to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Bishr ibn Salm narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Malik ibn al-Harith, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it. We do not know of anyone narrating the hadith of al-A'mash, from Umarah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, nor the hadith of al-A'mash, from Malik ibn al-Harith, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, except Qays."
"1921","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Malik ibn al-Harith, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No one is more jealous than Allah, and for that reason He has forbidden shameful acts, the apparent and the hidden; and no one loves praise more than Allah. We do not know of Malik ibn al-Harith narrating from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, except these two hadiths."
"1922","Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke in the morning he would say: We have entered the morning upon the natural disposition of Islam, the word of sincerity, and the religion of our father Ibrahim, sincerely devoted to Him in religion; and when evening came he would say the like of that. Al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah said: And Zubayd narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his father, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ."
"1923","Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn al-Rawwas narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Your permission to enter upon me is that you lift the curtain, and that you see my private state, until I forbid you. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from Abdullah except with this isnad, and he is Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, not al-Nakha'i. Both Ibrahim al-Nakha'i and Ibrahim ibn Suwayd narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid. As for what Mansur, al-Hakam and al-A'mash narrated from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, it is Ibrahim al-Nakha'i; and as for what al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah narrated, it is Ibrahim ibn Suwayd."
"1924","Abd al-A'la ibn Wasil al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his father, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever begs while he has what suffices him will come on the Day of Resurrection with scratches — or marks — on his face. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is his sufficiency? He said: Fifty dirhams or its equivalent in gold. Yahya ibn Adam said: I knew that Shu'bah was not pleased with Hakim ibn Jubayr, so I said to him: Sufyan narrated it to me from Zubayd, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his father in this manner, but he did not say ""from Abdullah"". This Hakim ibn Jubayr is a Kufan man, weak in hadith; as for Zubayd, he did not narrate this hadith in musnad form from Abdullah."
"1925","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his father, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not a slanderer, nor one who curses much, nor obscene, nor foul-mouthed. This hadith was narrated from al-Hasan ibn Amr with this isnad by Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash and Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra."
"1926","Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, that he narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, saying this or something like it. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman, except Hafs ibn Ghiyath."
"1927","Sa'id ibn Bahr al-Qaratisî narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from al-A'mash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, prayers and good words; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings — and he mentioned the hadith of the tashahhud in full. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from al-A'mash, from Umarah, with this isnad, except Za'idah."
"1928","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Umarah, from Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah, that al-Ash'ath ibn Qays came to him on the day of Ashura while he was eating lunch, so he said: Come to lunch. He said: Is today not the day of Ashura? He replied: Do you know what the day of Ashura is? The day of Ashura is only a day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast before Ramadan was revealed; when Ramadan was revealed, it was abandoned."
"1929","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Masruqi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Muhayyah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid who said: I said to Abdullah — or it was said to Abdullah: Some people stone the Jamrah from above al-Aqabah. So Abdullah stoned from the interior of the valley and said: Thus, by the One besides whom there is no god, did the one stoned it upon whom Surah al-Baqarah was revealed."
"1930","Al-Ma'rur ibn Suwayd from Abdullah: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah al-Yashkuri, from al-Ma'rur ibn Suwayd, from Abdullah who said: Umm Habibah said: O Allah, bless me in my husband the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and in my father Abu Sufyan, and in my brother Mu'awiyah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have asked Allah for fixed lifespans and apportioned provisions, none of which will be hastened before its term. Had you asked Allah the Mighty and Majestic to grant you health — or to protect you from punishment in the Fire and punishment in the grave — it would have been better, or superior. He said: And monkeys and pigs were mentioned, so I said: Were they from what was transformed of the Children of Israel? He said: Allah, blessed and exalted, never destroyed a people and left them offspring or descendants; monkeys and pigs existed, I think, before that. We do not know of these words being narrated from Abdullah except with this isnad."
"1931","Silah ibn Zufar from Abdullah: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Silah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that al-Aqib and al-Sayyid came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he wanted to invoke mutual curses with them, so one of them said to his companion: Let us not invoke curses with him, for if he is a prophet and we invoke curses with him, neither we nor our descendants after us will prosper. They said to him: We will give you what you ask; send with us a trustworthy man, and send with us none but a trustworthy one. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall certainly send with you a truly trustworthy man. He said: Stand, O Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. When he stood, he said: This is the trustee of this ummah. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from Abdullah except with this isnad."
"1932","Khishf ibn Malik from Abdullah: Abu Kurayb and Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, both saying: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Khishf ibn Malik, from Abdullah who said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the severity of the heat of the ground, but he did not relieve our complaint. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith with this isnad except Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham, from Sufyan."
"1933","Taliq ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from Khishf ibn Malik, from Abdullah, in marfu' form, that he fixed the blood money for accidental killing in five categories. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from Abdullah in marfu' form except with this isnad."
"1934","Zadhan from Abdullah: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadhan, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ."
"1935","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Husayn al-Khulqani, from Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadhan, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has travelling angels who convey to me greetings from my ummah. Husayn said in his hadith: Allah has angels who roam the roads conveying greetings to me from my ummah. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from Abdullah except through this channel with this isnad."
"1936","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadhan, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah has travelling angels who convey to me greetings from my ummah. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My life is good for you — you narrate and it is narrated to you; and my death is good for you — your deeds are presented to me, and whatever good I see I praise Allah for, and whatever evil I see I seek Allah's forgiveness for you. The latter part of this hadith: we do not know of it being narrated from Abdullah except through this channel with this isnad."
"1937","Abdullah ibn Ma'qil ibn Muqarrin from Abdullah: Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim ibn al-Jazari, from Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam, from Abdullah ibn Ma'qil who said: My father and I entered upon Abdullah, and my father said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Remorse is repentance? He said: Yes. This hadith has been narrated by more than one from Abd al-Karim, and we do not know of Abdullah ibn Ma'qil narrating except this hadith."
"1938","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn Ma'qil, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Remorse is repentance. We heard this hadith only from Abd al-Wahid, from Abu Awanah."
"1939","Abu Fakhirrah from Abdullah: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhirah, from his father, from Ibn Mas'ud who said: The first to reduce the takbir was al-Walid ibn Uqbah. So Abdullah said: They reduced it — may Allah diminish them. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying takbir every time he bowed, every time he prostrated, and every time he rose."
"1940","Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-A'mash, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhirah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud."
"1941","And Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated it to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhirah, from his father, from Abdullah who said: I took seventy surahs from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) . We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from al-A'mash, from Thuwayr, except Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi."
"1942","Hammam ibn al-Harith from Abdullah: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam, from Abdullah who said: Whoever goes to a soothsayer or a magician and believes him in what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ."
"1943","Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Abu Zayd Sa'id ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mis'ar and al-Mas'udi, from Wabarah, from Hammam, from Abdullah who said: Bathing on Friday is part of the Sunnah. This hadith has been narrated from al-Mas'udi and from Mis'ar through various channels, but we mentioned it from the hadith of Shu'bah."
"1944","Ahmad ibn Sinan and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Makhlad narrated to us, both saying: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, from al-A'mash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from al-Aswad and Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was feverish, so I placed my hand on him and said: O Messenger of Allah, how severe your fever is; you are afflicted with a severe ailment. He said: Yes, I am afflicted as two men of you are afflicted. There is no believing servant, male or female, who falls ill with an illness except that Allah sheds his sins as leaves fall — or are shed — from a tree. This hadith has been narrated by others besides Sharik, from al-A'mash, from Umarah, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah; and Sharik added, from al-A'mash, from Umarah, from al-Aswad and Hammam."
"1945","Ibrahim from Masruq; Masruq from Abdullah: Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf informed us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who strikes faces, tears garments, and calls with the call of ignorance. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Abdullah, except Zubayd."
"1946","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Zubayd, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Usury has seventy-odd doors, and idolatry is like that. We did not hear anyone narrate this hadith with this isnad in musnad form except Amr ibn Ali."
"1947","Al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Rukhami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Amr, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i who said: Masruq ibn al-Ajda' was sitting with al-Dahhak ibn Qays, and with him was Umarah ibn Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt. Al-Dahhak wanted to employ Masruq in some of his works, so Umarah ibn Uqbah said to him: Would you employ a man from the remnants of Uthman's killers? So Masruq said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud narrated to us — and he was with us trustworthy in hadith, not a liar — that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought your father, he ordered his neck to be struck. He said: Who will care for the children after me? He said: The Fire. So what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed for you is sufficient. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from Abdullah except through this channel with this isnad."
"1948","Al-Sha'bi from Masruq from Abdullah: Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be after me twelve caliphs — I think he said: the number of the chiefs of the Children of Israel."
"1949","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari and Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, both saying: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it. We do not know of an isnad for this hadith from Abdullah better than this isnad, although the scholars have spoken about Mujalid."
"1950","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, from Masruq, from Abdullah, in marfu' form, he said: The judge will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and made to stand at the edge of Hell; if he is ordered to be taken and pushed, he will fall into it for seventy autumns. We do not know of anyone narrating it in musnad form from Mujalid except Yahya ibn Sa'id."
"1951","He said: And I heard Amr ibn Ali mentioning this hadith from Yahya ibn Sa'id and Muhammad ibn Fudayl, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ; and I think Amr ibn Ali carried the hadith of Ibn Fudayl upon the hadith of Yahya regarding the marfu' narration, for I did not hear anyone narrate it in marfu' form from Ibn Fudayl except Amr ibn Ali, who combined Yahya and Ibn Fudayl in it."
"1952","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us, both saying: Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban al-Anazi narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Amir, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: When Abu Jahl was brought, dragged to the well, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had Abu Talib been alive, he would have known — or learned — that our swords have been clad with the noblest. We do not know of anyone narrating it from Mujalid except Hibban ibn Ali, nor do we know of anyone narrating it from him except Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban."
"1953","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti and Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Muwatiyah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at hunger in the faces of his Companions and said: Rejoice, for there will come upon you a time when a bowl of tharid will be brought to one of you in the morning and the like of it in the evening. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we be better then? He said: Rather, you today are better than you will be then. We do not know of anyone narrating it from Mujalid except Muhammad ibn Fudayl, nor from Ibn Fudayl except this Muhammad ibn Ja'far, and he was not corroborated in it."
"1954","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The millstone of Islam will turn, meaning, after thirty-five years; if they perish, then by the path of those who perished, and if they remain, their affair will remain for them for seventy years."
"1955","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: He would sometimes narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his face would change colour, and he would say: Something like this, or close to this. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from Firas except Abu Awanah, nor from Abu Awanah except Yahya ibn Ghaylan."
"1956","Mahmud ibn Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The upper hand is better than the lower hand; begin with those you support — your mother and your father, your sister and your brother. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from the hadith of al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, except through the hadith of Ibn Abi Layla and al-Sari ibn Isma'il."
"1957","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: One day he narrated, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and he was seized with trembling, and his garments trembled — then he said: Something like this, or thus."
"1958","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: The first grandmother to inherit in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a grandmother whose son was alive. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith except Muhammad ibn Salim, and he was not corroborated in it; and this Muhammad ibn Salim is lenient in hadith."
"1959","Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Tha'labah narrated to us, he said: Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, from al-Sari ibn Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: It is part of the Sunnah for a man to say in his bowing: Glory be to my Lord the Almighty, three times, and in his prostration: Glory be to my Lord the Most High, three times. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from Masruq, from Abdullah, except through this channel; and this al-Sari ibn Isma'il is not strong."
"1960","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Sari ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man of the desert, well-off, and I have a mother and a father, a brother and a sister, a paternal uncle and a paternal aunt, a maternal uncle and a maternal aunt; which of them is most entitled to my maintaining ties? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your mother and your father, your sister and your brother, and the nearest, the nearest."
"1961","Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Amir ibn Mudrik narrated to us, he said: al-Sari ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was on a high place of the ground until I sat facing his face — or my face at his knees — and I seized the solitude of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, which sins are greatest? He turned away from me until I said it three times, then he turned his face to me and said: That you set up a rival to Allah while He created you. Then I said: Then what? He said: That you kill your child lest he eat — or share food — with you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then what? Or then what? He said: That you commit adultery with your neighbour's wife. Then he stretched out his hand and recited: {And those who do not call upon another god with Allah} to the end of the verse. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from al-Sha'bi with this isnad except al-Sari ibn Isma'il; al-Sari is not strong, though al-Zuhri and a large group of scholars narrated from him."
"1962","Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Amir ibn Mudrik narrated to us, he said: al-Sari ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, I love you — I think he said: By Allah, I love you — saying it three times. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is this one swearing upon what he swore? The man said: I am, O Messenger of Allah. So he said: Go, for you are with those you love; upon you is what you earned, and upon Allah is what you sought. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, except al-Sari ibn Isma'il, and our remarks about al-Sari ibn Isma'il have already preceded."
"1963","Abdullah ibn Murrah and others of Masruq's companions from Masruq: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, both saying: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood of a man who testifies that there is no god but Allah is not lawful except for one of three: a life for a life, the married adulterer, and the one who abandons his religion and separates from the community."
"1964","And al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated it to us, he said: Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from Abdullah except through this channel, except one hadith."
"1965","Al-Fadl narrated it to us, from Aswad ibn Amir, from Zuhayr, from al-A'mash, from Muslim — he being Abu al-Duha — from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it. The hadith of Muslim is not preserved; it is only preserved from the hadith of Abdullah ibn Murrah."
"1966","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: He is not of us who strikes cheeks, tears garments, and calls with the call of ignorance."
"1967","Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard al-A'mash narrating it from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among palm trees when some Jews confronted him and asked him about the soul. He stood still for a while, and we thought revelation was coming to him, then he said: {And they ask you about the soul; say: The soul is of the affair of my Lord, and you have not been given of knowledge except little}. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah, except Ibn Idris; others besides Ibn Idris narrate it from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah."
"1968","Amr ibn Ali and Ibrahim ibn Abdullah narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The two eyes commit adultery, the two hands commit adultery, the two feet commit adultery, and the private part commits adultery. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from Asim, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah in marfu' form, except Hammam."
"1969","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah, Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim and Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: I took seventy surahs from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ."
"1970","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Abu al-Musawir al-Fadl ibn Musawir narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it. We do not know of anyone narrating it from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, except Abu Awanah and Shayban."
"1971","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking one another's necks; and no man shall be seized for his father's offence, nor for his brother's offence."
"1972","And Isa ibn Musa al-Sami narrated it to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it. Parts of these words have been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various channels with different wordings, and part of its wording has been narrated from Abdullah through another channel; but we do not know of it being narrated with this wording except through this channel."
"1973","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salam to his right and to his left in prayer. This hadith is narrated from others besides Musa, from al-Thawri, from Jabir, from Muslim, from Masruq, from Abdullah."
"1974","Nasr ibn Ali, Muhammad ibn Mirdas and al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Jazari narrated to us — Nasr said: Sahl ibn Yusuf informed us, and the other two said: Sahl ibn Yusuf narrated to us — from al-Hajjaj, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salam in prayer to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. We preserve no hadith of al-Hajjaj, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, except through the hadith of Sahl from him."
"1975","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: The truthful, the believed one said: Selling milk-retained animals is deception, and deception is not lawful. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from Abu al-Duha except through the hadith of Jabir."
"1976","Nasr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us — Nasr said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad informed us, and Muhammad ibn Yahya said: Abu Abd al-Samad Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us — he said: Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Muslim, meaning Abu al-Duha, who said: I was with Masruq in a house containing an image of Maryam. Masruq said: Is this an image of Khosrau? I said: No, but it is an image of Maryam. So Masruq said: I heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ud saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers. This hadith has been narrated by al-A'mash, Mansur and Husayn, from Muslim, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ."
"1977","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur. And al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated it to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Muslim, who said: Masruq said: We were with Abdullah when a man came to us while Abdullah was reclining, and said: I have come to you from the mosque, and some people met me at the gates of Kindah saying: The Smoke — or the sign of the Smoke will come, seizing the breath of the disbelievers, while the believer is seized like a cold. Abdullah became angry and sat up and said: O people, whoever of you knows something, let him say what he knows; whoever does not know, let him say: Allah knows best. For the knowledge of one of you, when asked about what he does not know, is to say: Allah knows best. Allah, blessed and exalted, said to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {Say: I ask you no reward for it, nor am I of the pretenders}. The sign of the Smoke has already passed. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw people turning away, he said: O Allah, seven years like the seven of Yusuf. So a famine seized the people, consuming everything, until they ate carrion and skins. Then Abu Sufyan came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, you came commanding obedience to Allah and ties of kinship, yet your people have perished, so supplicate to Allah for them. Then Abdullah recited this verse: {So watch for the day when the sky brings} until {Indeed you will return}. He said: So it was lifted. Abdullah said: The punishment of the Hereafter was lifted. The sign of the Smoke has passed; the Mighty Seizure and the Inevitable were on the day of Badr and have passed, as has the sign of Rome. He said: We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith except Muslim, from Masruq, from Abdullah."
"1978","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us, he said: Fitr narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq who said: I heard Ibn Mas'ud saying: Five have already passed: the splitting of the moon, and {Alif Lam Mim; the Romans have been defeated}, and {The day when the sky brings a clear smoke}, and {The day We seize with the greatest seizure}, and the day of Badr."
"1979","Isa ibn Musa al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman and Husayn, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from Shu'bah with this isnad except Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr; more than one has narrated it from al-A'mash, and it has also been narrated from Husayn without the hadith of Shu'bah."
"1980","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq who said: I entered upon Ibn Mas'ud while he was with Abu Musa, and Hudhayfah was with him. Hudhayfah said: O Abdullah ibn Qays, you were sent to the people of Basra as a governor and a teacher, and they took from your manners and your recitation. Ibn Mas'ud said: There is no verse of the Qur'an except that I know when it was revealed and concerning what it was revealed; and had I known anyone more knowledgeable of the Book of Allah than me, reachable by camel, I would have journeyed to him."
"1981","Al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Rukhami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) , when bowing or prostrating, would say: Glory be to You and with Your praise; I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You. We do not know of Hammad narrating from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, except this hadith with this isnad."
"1982","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: The moon split in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the idolaters said: This is magic — but look and ask them; so they asked Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) . Abu Bakr al-Bazzar said: I do not have more than this in it."
"1983","Amr ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Jumay' narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salam in prayer to his right: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen, and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. We do not know of al-Mughirah narrating from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, except three hadiths."
"1984","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, Amr ibn Ali and Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us, saying: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has supporters from among the prophets, and my supporter among them is my father and the intimate friend of my Lord. Then he said: {Indeed the most entitled of people to Ibrahim are those who followed him, and this Prophet and those who believed} to the end of the verse. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith in connected form except Abu Ahmad, from al-Thawri; others besides Abu Ahmad narrated it from al-Thawri, from his father, from Abu al-Duha, from Abdullah."
"1985","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer and gave salam to his right until the whiteness of his left cheek could be seen: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. He said: So Abdullah said: I have not forgotten since, among what I forgot."
"1986","Yahya ibn Waththab from Masruq from Abdullah: al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Ja'far al-Ahmar and Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, both saying: Yahya ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: Sleep was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Sleep; when you wake, do good. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from Isra'il with this isnad, attributing it in musnad form to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except Yahya ibn al-Mundhir."
"1987","Ibrahim ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us. And Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Masruq, from Abdullah, in marfu' form, he said: The impure does not expiate the impure; rather, the pure expiates the impure. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from Abd al-A'la except with this isnad."
"1988","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Bilal while he had a heap of dates with him, and said: What is this, O Bilal? He said: I am storing it for your guests. He said: Do you not fear that it may become smoke for you in the fire of Hell? Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear decrease from the Possessor of the Throne. Qays narrated this hadith thus, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya, from Masruq, from Abdullah; Abu Ghassan and Asim narrated it from him. Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated it from Qays, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya, from Masruq, from A'ishah. Isa ibn Musa al-Sami narrated it to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us."
"1989","Abdullah ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: I know the paired surahs which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite. Ibn Raja narrated this hadith; I have not seen it with me from the hadith of Ubaydullah ibn Musa, nor did I hear anyone mentioning it except from Ibn Raja, and it is known through him. End of the eighteenth juz and beginning of the nineteenth; praise be to Allah."
"1990","Continuation of the hadith of Masruq: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Ali and Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Qattan narrated to us, both saying: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has supporters from among the prophets, and my supporter among them is my father and the intimate friend of my Lord — meaning Ibrahim, peace be upon him — then he recited: {Indeed the most entitled of people to Ibrahim are those who followed him, and this Prophet and those who believed; and Allah is the Guardian of the believers}. We do not know of this hadith being narrated from Abdullah except with this isnad in connected form."
"1991","Isa ibn Musa al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Husayn — meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman — and Sulayman — meaning al-A'mash — from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers. A group narrated this hadith from al-A'mash; we do not know of anyone combining Husayn and Sulayman except Shu'bah, nor do we know of anyone narrating it from Shu'bah except Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr."
"1992","And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"1993","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Ma'n — meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman — he said: I heard my father saying: I asked Masruq: Who informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the jinn on the night they listened to the Qur'an? He said: My father — meaning Ibn Mas'ud — narrated to me that only a tree informed him of them. Abu Usamah narrated this hadith from Mis'ar, from Ma'n; Ibn Uyaynah differed with him, narrating it from Mis'ar, from Amr ibn Murrah."
"1994","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Mas'ud from his father; al-Qasim from his father from his grandfather; Abu Ishaq from him: Ahmad ibn Sinan, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan and Muhammad ibn Ubadah al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a snake, it is as if he killed a disbeliever. We do not know of Abu Ishaq narrating from al-Qasim, from his father, from Abdullah, except this hadith."
"1995","Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir from al-Qasim: Muhammad ibn Humayd wrote to me informing me in his letter that Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to him, he said: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Mansur — meaning Ibn al-Mu'tamir — from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am pleased for my ummah with what Ibn Umm Abd is pleased with for it, and I dislike for my ummah what Ibn Umm Abd dislikes for it. We do not know of Mansur narrating in musnad form from al-Qasim, from his father, from Abdullah, except this hadith; nor do we know of it being narrated in musnad form except by Amr ibn Abi Qays, from the hadith of Muhammad ibn Humayd, from Harun. It has been narrated from Mansur, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, as mursal."
"1996","Al-A'mash from al-Qasim: Ali ibn Muslim al-Tusi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-A'mash, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah who said: You saw me when I was the sixth of six, with no Muslim on the face of the earth besides us. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from al-A'mash with this isnad except Abu Ubaydah ibn Ma'n, nor from him except his son."
"1997","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Uthman narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from his grandfather Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abdullah, there will come after me people who delay prayer past its times. Abdullah said: I said: How do you command me, O Messenger of Allah? He said: O Ibn Umm Abd, if you reach them, there is no obedience to a created being in disobedience to the Creator. We do not know of these words being narrated from Abdullah except with this isnad."
"1998","Simak from al-Qasim: Yusuf ibn Musa and Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, both saying: al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on an expedition, and we travelled late into one night. I said: If only you would dismount so we could rest. He said: Who will guard us? He said: I shall guard you. So they slept, and I slept as they slept, until the sun rose. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, performed ablution, and we performed ablution for the morning prayer, then we prayed the morning prayer in the forenoon. Za'idah and Yazid ibn Ata narrated this hadith from Simak, from al-Qasim."
"1999","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Anmati narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Simak — meaning Ibn Harb — from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that the Children of Israel appointed a caliph over them after Musa, peace be upon him. He stood praying one night in the moonlight above Bayt al-Maqdis, then recalled deeds he had done, so he went out and let himself down by a rope. In the morning the rope was left hanging in the mosque while he was gone. He went until he came to people on the seashore whom he found making bricks — or manufacturing bricks — and asked them how they were paid for these bricks. They told him, so he made bricks with them, eating from the work of his hands. When prayer time came he would stand praying. The workers reported to their overseer that among them was a man doing such-and-such. He sent for him but he refused to come to him three times. Then he came to him riding his mount; when he saw him he fled, and he followed him but he outran him. He said: Give me a moment to speak to you. So he stood until he spoke to him, and told him his story. When he told him that he had been a king and had fled out of fear of Allah, he said: I think I shall join you. So he followed him, and they worshipped Allah until they both died at Rumaylat Misr. Abdullah said: Had I been there, I would have found their graves from the description the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described to us. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from Simak, from al-Qasim, from his father, from Abdullah, except Amr ibn Abi Qays; al-Mas'udi narrated it from Simak, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, without mentioning al-Qasim."
"2000","Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq from al-Qasim: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad Abu Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud."
"2001","And Muhammad ibn al-Harith ibn Isma'il al-Khazzaz narrated it to us, he said: Sayyar ibn Hatim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I met Ibrahim, peace be upon him, in the seventh heaven. He said: O Muhammad, convey greetings to your ummah from me, and tell them that Paradise has sweet water and wholesome drink, that it contains open plains, and that the planting of its trees is: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest."
"2002","And Abu Kamil narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it — but he did not say ""from al-Qasim, from his father, from Abdullah"". We do not know of these words being narrated from Abdullah except through this channel with this isnad."
"2003","Ishaq ibn Buhlul narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salih al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us this supplication: O Allah, I am Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maidservant; my forelock is in Your hand; Your decree concerning me is carried out; Your judgement concerning me is executed. I ask You by every name with which You have named Yourself, or revealed in Your Book, or taught to any of Your creation, or kept to Yourself in the knowledge of the unseen with You, to make the Qur'an the spring of my heart, the light of my chest, the dispeller of my sorrow, and the remover of my grief — except that Allah removes his grief and replaces his sorrow with joy. They said: O Messenger of Allah, should we learn these words? He said: Yes, whoever hears them should learn them."
"2004","Umar ibn Qays from al-Qasim: Ali ibn Harb al-Junday Saburi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abi Hawdhah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Qays — meaning al-Masir — narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When the two sellers disagree and there is no proof between them, the word is what the seller says, or they annul the sale. We heard this hadith only from Ali ibn Harb with this isnad; we do not know of anyone narrating it from Umar ibn Qays except Amr ibn Abi Qays."
"2005","Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman from al-Qasim: Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, from Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The millstone of Islam will turn after thirty-five, or thirty-six, or thirty-seven; if they perish, then by the path of those who perished, and if they remain — or there remains — their religion will remain for them for seventy years."
"2006","Mujalid from al-Qasim: And al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated it to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Mujalid, he said: al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"2007","Al-Fadl only narrated it to us from al-Aswad ibn Amir, from Sharik, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these words. Sharik said: Then Mujalid narrated to me, he said: al-Qasim narrated to me, from his father, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it. We do not know of Mujalid narrating a musnad hadith from al-Qasim except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it from him except Sharik."
"2008","Al-Harith ibn Hasirah from al-Qasim: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Hasirah, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — meaning on the day of Hunayn — when the people scattered, and I remained with him among eighty men of the Muhajirun and the Ansar, they being those upon whom Allah sent down tranquillity. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon his mule, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hand me a handful of dust. He threw it at their faces, and their eyes filled with dust. The Muhajirun and the Ansar advanced with their swords in their right hands as if they were shooting stars, and the idolaters turned fleeing."
"2009","Amr ibn Bishr al-Naji narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Hasirah, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: How would you feel if a quarter of the people of Paradise were for you, and three quarters for the rest of people? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: How would you feel if a third of it? They said: That is more. He said: How would you feel if half? They said: That is more. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows; my ummah among them is eighty rows. We do not know of these two hadiths being narrated from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud except with this isnad."
"2010","Ata ibn al-Sa'ib from al-Qasim: al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, he said: Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: A man of the People of the Book came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about resemblance. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the man's fluid dominates, the resemblance prevails; when the woman's fluid dominates, the resemblance prevails. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from al-Qasim, from his father, from Abdullah, except Ata ibn al-Sa'ib; nor do we recall anyone narrating it from Ata except Abu Kudaynah."
"2011","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman from al-Qasim: Ali ibn Sahl al-Mada'ini narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Mindal narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla — he being Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla — from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah."
"2012","And Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Qattan narrated it to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Mindal narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah — and the wording is that of Yahya ibn Adam — who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me placing my left hand over my right in prayer, so he said: Place your right hand over your left. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from al-Qasim, from his father, from Abdullah, except Ibn Abi Layla."
"2013","Mahmud ibn Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Isa ibn al-Mukhtar, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the two sellers disagree with no proof between them, the word is what the seller says, or they annul the sale. This hadith is only known from the hadith of Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Qasim, except what Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated from Umar ibn Qays al-Masir, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman; more than one has narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Layla."
"2014","Al-Mas'udi from al-Qasim: Ubaydullah — a man of the descendants of al-Mughirah ibn Muslim, a companion of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi, a man of concealment and trustworthiness — narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I said: There is no power nor strength except through Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know its interpretation? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: There is no averting from disobedience to Allah except through Allah's protection, and no strength for obedience to Allah except through Allah's help. We heard this hadith in connected form from al-Qasim, from his father, from Abdullah, only through this channel."
"2015","And al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated it to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Khirash ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from al-Mas'udi, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud — but he did not say ""from al-Qasim, from his father""; rather, he narrated it in mursal form."
"2016","Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Mus'ab ibn Sallam narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj — meaning Ibn Artah — from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, in marfu' form, he said: When a man honours his brother, he only honours his Lord. We do not know of these words being narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this isnad; Mus'ab ibn Sallam is not strong, though more than one narrated from him, a Kufan man."
"2017","Jabir from al-Qasim: Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought captives, and he would give to a household together, disliking to separate them. We do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from al-Qasim except Jabir; more than one narrated it from Jabir."
"2018","Abu al-Malih from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah from his father: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim and al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, both saying: Shabbabah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hudhali narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Malih narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father who said: On the day of Badr I came upon Abu Jahl while iron armour covered him as if it were an onion, and he had been seated disabled. I took his sword; he raised his head and said: O little shepherd of Makkah? So I struck him with my sword until he grew cold. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I killed Abu Jahl. Aqil, a captive with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: You lie; you did not kill him. I said: Rather, you are the foul liar, O enemy of Allah; by Allah, I did kill him. He said: What is his mark? I said: On his thigh a ring like the ring of such-and-such, for something he mentioned — meaning a mark on his thigh. He said: You spoke the truth. We do not know of Abu al-Malih narrating from Abd al-Rahman, from his father, except this hadith."
"2019","Al-Hasan ibn Sa'd from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah from his father: Muhammad ibn al-Ala Abu Kurayb and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, both saying: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None punishes with fire except the Lord of the Fire."
"2020","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, both saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, from al-Mas'udi, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey when he entered a thicket. A man took the eggs of a small red bird; the bird came fluttering over the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which of you distressed this bird by taking its eggs? A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I took its eggs. He said: Return them out of mercy to it. We preserve this hadith only with this isnad."
"2021","Simak ibn Harb from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah from his father: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are aided and conquests are opened for you; whoever of you reaches that, let him fear Allah, enjoin good and forbid evil. We do not know of this hadith being narrated with this wording from Abdullah except through this channel with this isnad."
"2022","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) : He cursed the eater of usury and its giver, its scribe and its two witnesses. These words have been narrated from Abdullah through more than one channel."
"2023","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of one who aids his people in wrongdoing is like a camel that falls into a well and pulls itself out by its tail. We do not know of these words being narrated from Abdullah except through this channel."
"2024","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: May Allah brighten a man who hears a hadith from us and conveys it as he heard it, for many a conveyed one retains more than the hearer."
"2025","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in a red tent among some forty men, and he said: You are aided and conquests are opened for you; whoever of you reaches that, let him fear Allah, enjoin good and forbid evil. Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"2026","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Sufyan — meaning al-Thawri — narrated to us, from Simak, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, that he said: Two bargains in one bargain are not valid. He said: And the Messenger of Allah commanded us to perform ablution thoroughly. We heard this hadith only from Muhammad ibn Uthman, from his father; Muhammad ibn Uthman brought out to us a book which he mentioned was his father's book containing this hadith."
"2027","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, from Sharik, from Simak, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two bargains in one bargain. Sharik narrated this hadith in musnad form with this isnad."
"2028","Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah from his father: Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ."
"2029","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Mihran ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah — I think from his father — in marfu' form, he said: May Allah brighten a man who hears a hadith from us and conveys it as he heard it, for many a conveyed one retains more than the hearer. The hadith of Isma'il from Abdullah ibn Umayr: we do not know of anyone narrating it in musnad form except Mihran from him."
"2030","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrating from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking one another's necks. We preserve no hadith about Abdullah except with this isnad."
"2031","2021 - Ali ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Reviling the Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief. And these words have been reported from Abd Allah through more than one chain."
"2032","Murrah al-Hamdani from Abd Allah ibn Masud. 2022 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Talhah informed us, from Zubayd, from Murrah, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They kept us busy from the middle prayer until the sun set; may Allah fill their graves and their houses with fire. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abd Allah except through this chain with this isnad."
"2033","2023 - Umar ibn Shabbah narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Murrah, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will be gathered barefoot, naked, uncircumcised. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abd Allah except through this chain, and I think Umar ibn Shabbah erred in it, for no one corroborated him in it; rather with al-Thawri these words are from al-Mughirah ibn al-Numan, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas. And I think the text of one hadith entered into the isnad of another hadith, and with al-Thawri, from Zubayd, from Murrah, from Abd Allah there is no musnad hadith."
"2034","2024 - Abdah ibn Abd Allah and al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, they said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us, from al-Suddi, from Murrah, from Abd Allah - Shubah said: he raised it, and I do not raise it -: If a man at Adan Abyan intended him with evil, Allah would make him taste a painful punishment, meaning regarding the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: And whoever intends therein deviation with wrongdoing, We will make him taste a painful punishment. And we do not know anyone who reported this hadith from Shubah with this wording except Yazid ibn Harun."
"2035","2025 - Abdah ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Ishaq informed us, from al-Sabbah ibn Muhammad, from Murrah al-Hamdani, from Abd Allah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Feel true shyness before Allah. He said: We feel shy, and praise be to Allah. He said: That is not it; rather whoever feels true shyness before Allah, let him guard the head and what it retains, and guard the belly and what it contains, and remember death and decay; whoever does that has felt true shyness before Allah."
"2036","2026 - Abdah ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd informed us, he said: Aban ibn Ishaq informed us, from al-Sabbah ibn Muhammad, from Murrah, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, gives the world to whom He loves and whom He does not love, and He gives religion only to whom He loves. By Him in whose Hand is my soul, no servant submits until his heart submits, and no servant believes until his neighbor is safe from his harms. They said: What are his harms? He said: His oppression and wrongdoing. No servant earns unlawful wealth then gives it in charity that it is accepted from him, nor spends it that it is blessed for him, nor leaves it behind his back except it will be his provision to the Fire. Allah does not erase evil with evil, but erases evil with good; filth does not erase filth. Whoever earns wealth unlawfully then puts it in its right place, it is better for him not to rob the orphan and clothe the widow; whoever earns unlawful wealth and puts it in other than its right place, that is the incurable disease; whoever earns lawful wealth and puts it in its right place, his example is like rain that falls, and he mentioned a word I have forgotten. And this Aban ibn Ishaq is a Kufan man, and al-Sabbah ibn Muhammad is not well known; we only mentioned it with its defect because we did not preserve his words from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain with this isnad. Aban ibn Ishaq was reported from by Abd Allah ibn Numayr, Muhammad ibn Ubayd, and Yala ibn Ubayd."
"2037","2027 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Murrah, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angel has a touch and Satan has a touch; the angel's touch is promise of good and warning against evil, and Satan's touch is promise of evil, I think he said: and warning against good. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abd Allah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain with this isnad, and others reported it from other than Abu al-Ahwas as mawquf."
"2038","2028 - Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Ibn al-Asbahani that he informed him, from Murrah, from Abd Allah who said: Our beloved and our Prophet, may my father be ransom for him and myself for him, was announced to us before his death by six days; when parting drew near he gathered us in the house of our mother Aishah and looked at us and his eyes shed tears, then he said: Welcome to you, may Allah greet you, guard you, shelter you, help you, raise you, guide you, provide for you, grant you success, keep you safe, accept you. I enjoin upon you fear of Allah, and I entrust you to Allah and leave Him as guardian over you. I am to you a clear warner, that you not exalt yourselves over Allah among His servants and lands, for Allah said to me and to you: That is the Home of the Hereafter, We assign it to those who do not desire exaltedness in the earth nor corruption, and the end is for the righteous. Then he said: Is there not in Hell a dwelling for the arrogant. Then he said: The term has drawn near and the return to Allah, and to Sidrat al-Muntaha, and to the Garden of Refuge, and the fullest cup and the Highest Companion - I think so - so we said: O Prophet of Allah, who will wash you then? He said: The nearest then nearest men of my household. We said: In what shall we shroud you? He said: In these clothes of mine if you wish, or in a Yemeni suit, or in Egyptian white. He said: We said: Who will pray over you among us? So we wept and he wept, and said: Gently, may Allah forgive you and reward you well for your Prophet. When you have washed me then placed me on my bed in this house of mine at the edge of my grave, leave me for a while, for the first to pray over me will be my friend and companion Jibril, then Mikail, then Israfil, then the Angel of Death with his soldiers, then the angels altogether, then enter upon me in groups and pray over me and send salutations; do not harm me with a wailing woman - I think he said - nor a screaming nor wailing one; let the men of my household begin prayer over me, then you after; convey salutations from yourselves to me, and whoever of my brothers is absent convey my salutations to him, and whoever enters your religion after me, I call you to witness that I send salutations upon myself and upon everyone who follows me in my religion from this day to the Day of Resurrection. We said: O Messenger of Allah, who will put you in your grave among us? He said: Men of my household with many angels whom you see from where you do not see them. And these words have been reported from Murrah from Abd Allah through more than one chain, and their isnads from Murrah from Abd Allah are close; Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani did not hear this from Murrah, it is only from one who informed him from Murrah, and I do not know anyone who reported it from Abd Allah other than Murrah."
"2039","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Alqamah al-Thaqafi from Abd Allah. 2029 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Alqamah who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Masud say: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from al-Hudaybiyah, and he mentioned that they camped on soft sandy ground - and dahas is sand - so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will guard us tonight? Bilal said: I will. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then you will sleep, or we will sleep. He said: So they slept until the sun rose, and people woke up, among them so-and-so and so-and-so, and among them Umar. He said: So we said: Speak up - meaning talk - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke and said: Do as you used to do. He said: So we did. He said: So do likewise with one who sleeps or forgets. He said: The camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) strayed, so I sought it and found its rope caught on a tree, so I brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he rode and we went. He said: When revelation descended upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) it weighed heavily upon him and we recognized that in him. He said: So he withdrew apart behind us, and began covering his head and it weighed heavily upon him until we knew revelation had been sent down upon him, then he came to us and informed us that there had been sent down upon him: Indeed We have granted you a clear victory. And we do not preserve this hadith with this wording except through this chain with this isnad."
"2040","2030 - Abdah ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam informed us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Walid, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Alqamah, from Abd Allah ibn Masud who said: There were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night he slept past the prayer until the sun rose two guides. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abd Allah except with this isnad."
"2041","Abd Allah ibn al-Harith from Abd Allah ibn Masud. 2031 - Bishr ibn Muadh al-Aqadi and al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, they said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Araj narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: On the day Allah spoke to Musa he wore a woolen cloak, a woolen outer garment, woolen trousers, a woolen cap, and sandals of undressed donkey skin. Abu Bakr said: The wording is that of Bishr ibn Muadh; we do not know this hadith reported from Abd Allah ibn Masud except with this isnad, and we do not know anyone who reported it except Khalaf ibn Khalifah."
"2042","2032 - al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Araj narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Abd Allah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will look at a bird in Paradise and desire it, and it will come to you roasted before you. And we do not know this hadith reported except from Abd Allah, and we do not know any path from Abd Allah except this path; this Humayd al-Araj is a Kufan man, not Humayd al-Makki who reported from Mujahid, and we do not know him reporting except from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, and he is Humayd ibn Ata."
"2043","2033 - Muhammad ibn Muawiyah ibn Malij narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Humayd al-Araj, he is Ibn Ata, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Abd Allah ibn Masud who said: When there was revealed: Who is it that will lend Allah a good loan, Abu al-Dahdah said: O Messenger of Allah, does Allah want a loan from us? He said: Yes, O Abu al-Dahdah. He said: I have lent my Lord my garden, a garden with six hundred palm trees. Then he walked until he came to the garden with Umm al-Dahdah among his family, and called her: O Umm al-Dahdah. She said: At your service. He said: Come out, for I have lent my Lord a garden with six hundred palm trees. And we do not know these words reported from Abd Allah except through this chain with this isnad, and we do not know anyone who reported it from Humayd except Khalaf ibn Khalifah."
"2044","2034 - Yusuf ibn Musa and Ibrahim ibn Ziyad narrated to us, they said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Araj narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Abd Allah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his prostration: My darkness and my shadow have prostrated to You, my heart has believed in You, I confess Your favor upon me; these are my hands and what I have earned against myself. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abd Allah except through this chain, and similar words with other than this wording have been reported from other than Abd Allah."
"2045","2035 - Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Jariyah ibn Harim narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Araj narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, raised, who said: Many a ragged man in two worn garments, paid no heed to, if he swears by Allah, Allah fulfills it. And we do not know these words reported from Abd Allah except with this isnad."
"2046","2036 - Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Jariyah ibn Harim narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Araj narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit and said: Amin, amin, amin, then he mentioned the hadith."
"2047","Umayr ibn Said from Abd Allah. 2037 - Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Umayr ibn Said, from Abd Allah who said: We used to say in prayer: Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon so-and-so, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is al-Salam, so say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. And we do not know that Umayr ibn Said reported from Abd Allah except this hadith, and more than one reported it from al-Hajjaj, from Umayr ibn Said, from Abd Allah as mawquf."
"2048","Zayd ibn Zaid from Abd Allah. 2038 - Ishaq ibn Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Sukkari and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, they said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Ismail al-Suddi, from al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham, from Zayd ibn Zaid, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should convey to me anything about any of my Companions, for I love to come out to you with a sound heart. And we do not know these words reported from Abd Allah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain, and we do not know anyone who reported it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abd Allah ibn Masud with this isnad."
"2049","Abu Hayyan from Abd Allah. 2039 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Husayn, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu Hayyan, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2050","2040 - And Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn al-Rawwas narrated it to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Husayn, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu Hayyan, from Abd Allah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Recite to me. I said: Shall I recite to you when it was revealed to you? Then he mentioned the hadith."
"2051","Kurdus ibn Abbas from Abd Allah. 2041 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Kurdus al-Thalabi, from Abd Allah ibn Masud who said: The chiefs of Quraysh passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while with him were Suhayb, Bilal, Ammar, Khabbab and the like among the weak Muslims, and they said: O Muhammad, drive them away; are you content with these among your people? Shall we follow these upon whom Allah has favored above us? Perhaps if you drive them away we will come to you. He said: Then this verse was revealed: And warn with it those who fear they will be gathered to their Lord, they have besides Him no protector nor intercessor, that they may fear; and do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening seeking His Face; nothing of their account is upon you nor anything of your account upon them, lest you drive them away and be among the wrongdoers. And we do not know these words reported from Abd Allah except through this chain with this isnad."
"2052","Al-Rabi ibn Umaylah from Abd Allah. 2042 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from his father, from Abd Allah, raised, who said: Usury, however much, returns to little. And we do not know anyone who reported these words from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abd Allah ibn Masud."
"2053","Al-Huzayl ibn Shurahbil from Abd Allah. 2043 - Musa ibn Abd Allah al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Shubah and Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu Qays, from al-Huzayl, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning a daughter, a son's daughter, and a full sister: for the daughter half, for the son's daughter a sixth completing two-thirds, and what remains for the full sister."
"2054","2044 - And Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Minjab narrated to us, from Ali ibn Mushir, from al-Amash, from Abu Qays, from al-Huzayl, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. And we do not know these words reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this isnad, from Abd Allah from him."
"2055","2045 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Qays, from al-Huzayl, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he cursed the tattooer and the one tattooed, and the one who joins hair and the one who asks for it."
"2056","2046 - Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Qays, from al-Huzayl, from Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined the two prayers while traveling. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abd Allah except with this isnad."
"2057","2047 - Ismail ibn Masud narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Abu Qays, from al-Huzayl, from Abd Allah, that a man bequeathed to a man a share of his wealth, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned him a sixth. And we do not know this hadith's words reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain with this isnad; Abu Qays is not strong, and Shubah, al-Thawri, al-Amash and others reported from him."
"2058","2048 - Bishr ibn Adam and Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us, they said: Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, from Huzayl, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: You are the most like of nations to the Children of Israel in manner, appearance and guidance. And we do not know that Abu Qays reported from Huzayl from Abd Allah except these hadiths raised."
"2059","Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah ibn Masud; Salamah ibn Kuhayl from him. 2049 - Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us, from Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so slept last night until morning. He said: That is a man in whose ears Satan has urinated. And we do not know anyone who reported it from al-Thawri, from Salamah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah except al-Qasim ibn Yazid and one other man."
"2060","2050 - Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, he said: my father Ismail ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to me, from his father, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud in prayer as he taught us a surah of the Quran: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. And we do not know this hadith reported from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah except through this chain."
"2061","2051 - Ibrahim ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from his father, from Salamah, from Abu al-Ahwas who said: Abd Allah said: They are only two: guidance and speech; the best speech is the speech of Allah, the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the worst matters are newly invented ones, and all that is coming is near."
"2062","Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah. 2052 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I disavow before every close friend his closeness, and had I taken a close friend I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend. And we do not know that Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl reported from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah except this hadith."
"2063","Abd Allah ibn Murrah from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah. 2053 - Amr ibn Abd Allah al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abd Allah ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I disavow before every close friend his closeness, and had I taken a close friend I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but your companion is the close friend of Allah, meaning himself. And we do not know that Abd Allah ibn Murrah reported from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah except this hadith."
"2064","Ali ibn al-Aqmar from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah. 2054 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Hour will not come except upon the worst of people. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abd Allah except through this chain with this isnad."
"2065","2055 - Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zara narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Masud say: The truest speech is the Book of Allah, the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the worst matters are newly invented ones, and every innovation is misguidance; hold to this Quran, for it is the banquet of Allah, so whoever of you can take from Allah's banquet let him do so, for knowledge is only by learning."
"2066","2056 - And Ishaq ibn Buhlul narrated it to us, he said: al-Walid ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, similarly."
"2067","Uqbah ibn Wassaj from al-Ahwas from Abd Allah. 2057 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Uqbah ibn Wassaj, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The merit of a man's prayer in congregation over his prayer alone is twenty-five, meaning twenty-five prayers. Thus Shubah reported it from Qatadah from Uqbah ibn Wassaj from Abu al-Ahwas; and Ibn Abi Arubah reported it from Qatadah from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congregational prayer exceeds a man's prayer alone by twenty-five fold."
"2068","2058 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us with it, he said: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah. And Hammam reported it from Qatadah from Muwarriq from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah."
"2069","Muwarriq al-Ijli from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah. 2059 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muwarriq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Congregational prayer exceeds a man's prayer alone by twenty-four fold, and it is the fifth, all of it like his prayer."
"2070","2060 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muwarriq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A woman's prayer in her inner chamber is better than her prayer in her house, and her prayer in her house is better than her prayer in her courtyard. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah except with this isnad."
"2071","2061 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muwarriq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The woman is awrah; when she goes out Satan looks at her, and she is closest to her Lord's Face while in the depths of her house."
"2072","2062 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. And the hadith of Muwarriq from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah, that the woman is awrah, we do not know anyone who reported it from Qatadah except Hammam."
"2073","2063 - al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muwarriq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman's prayer in her inner chamber is better than her prayer in her house, and her prayer in her house is better than her prayer in her courtyard."
"2074","2064 - And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The middle prayer is the Asr prayer."
"2075","2065 - And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The woman is awrah; when she leaves her house Satan looks at her. And these hadiths were brought out to us by al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad from a book he mentioned was his original, from Amr ibn Asim, inserted with one isnad; we objected to his hadith that the middle prayer is the Asr prayer, and these words were in the middle of the hadiths, and I saw no one corroborate al-Jarrah in this narration."
"2076","Abu Farwah from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah. 2066 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sanani and Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi narrated to us, they said: Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: Abu Farwah narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite on Friday: Alif Lam Mim, Tanzil, and Has there come. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Farwah from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah except through this chain with this isnad."
"2077","2067 - Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Ala al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Abu Nuaym Abd al-Rahman ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Husayn narrated to us, from Abu Farwah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salutations to his right and to his left, meaning in prayer. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Farwah from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah except through this chain; Abd al-Malik ibn Husayn is not strong, and a group reported from him and differed in his hadith."
"2078","Ata ibn al-Saib from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah. 2068 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, raised, who said: Congregational prayer exceeds a man's prayer alone by some twenty degrees. And we do not know that Ata ibn al-Saib reported anything musnad from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah except this hadith."
"2079","Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah. 2069 - Abu Kurayb and Ibrahim ibn Yusuf narrated to us, they said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Islam began strange and will return strange as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers. It was said: Who are the strangers? He said: Those who break away from tribes. And we do not know anyone who reported it from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah as musnad except al-Amash; Abu Khalid, Yusuf ibn Khalid and others reported it from al-Amash."
"2080","2070 - Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Absi Abu Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated to us, he said: Abthar narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the sermon of the tashahhud and the sermon of need. And we do not know anyone who reported it from al-Amash except Abthar."
"2081","2071 - Ahmad ibn Yazdad al-Khayyat al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah who said: In the days of ignorance we used to consider the tag-along to be a man who is invited then comes with one who was not invited. And we do not know anyone who reported it from al-Amash from Abu Ishaq with this isnad except Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar."
"2082","2072 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Had I taken a close friend from my ummah I would have taken Abu Bakr. And this hadith has been reported from Abu al-Ahwas through more than one chain."
"2083","2073 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: O Allah, I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity and sufficiency. And we do not preserve this hadith from Abd Allah except from the hadith of Abu al-Ahwas from him."
"2084","2074 - Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Tai narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me, for Satan does not take my form."
"2085","2075 - Amr ibn Abd Allah al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Waki narrated to us, from Israil and his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abd Allah with this wording except with this isnad."
"2086","2076 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, he said: Idris al-Awdi narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, raised, who said: The best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the best stories are the Book of Allah, the worst matters are newly invented ones, every innovation is bidah, reviling the Muslim is wickedness and fighting him is disbelief. And we do not know that Idris al-Awdi reported any musnad hadith from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah except this hadith, and we do not know anyone who reported it from Idris except Jarir; Muhammad ibn Jafar reported it from Musa ibn Uqbah from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah as musnad."
"2087","2077 - Salm ibn Junadah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, regarding the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: Had you spent all that is in the earth you would not have united their hearts, but Allah united them. He said: It was revealed about those who love one another for Allah. And we do not know anyone who reported it from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah except Fudayl ibn Ghazwan."
"2088","2078 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us. 2079 - And Khallad ibn Aslam narrated it to us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us; both mentioned it from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from his father, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah who said: They used to recite behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: You have confused the Quran for me. And we do not know anyone who reported it from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah except Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq."
"2089","2080 - Ubayd Allah ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: my uncle Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, and from Abu Ishaq al-Hajari, from Abd Allah, both raising the hadith, who said: When your servant comes to one of you with food, let him feed him from it or hand him some of it. And this hadith is only known from the hadith of al-Hajari from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah; Yaqub ibn Ibrahim combined from Sharik from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani and Abu Ishaq al-Hajari."
"2090","2081 - Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Bukhari narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Uways, meaning Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways, narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Quran was revealed upon seven letters; for every verse thereof is an outer and inner meaning; and he forbade a man to lie back - I think he said: in the mosque - placing one leg over the other. And we do not know this hadith reported except from the hadith of al-Hajari from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah; we do not know that Ibn Ajlan reported from al-Hajari anything but this hadith, and we do not know this hadith reported from Ibn Ajlan from Abu Ishaq except through this chain."
"2091","2082 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sanani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with people who stay back from Friday; I have intended to command a man to lead the people in prayer then stay behind and burn down the houses of people who stay back from Friday. And this hadith was reported from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas from Abd Allah by Mamar and Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah. The first volume of al-Bazzar's Musnad book is complete, and praise be to Allah as He deserves, and may Allah bless Muhammad His Prophet and servant and grant him peace. What follows at the beginning of the second, by Allah's power, is the Musnad of Suhayb ibn Sinan from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2092","Musnad of Suhayb ibn Sinan, may Allah be pleased with him. Musnad of Suhayb ibn Sinan from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ibn Umar from Suhayb. 2083 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Nabil, keeper of the cloak, from Ibn Umar, from Suhayb, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Quba and people came to him and began greeting him while he was praying, and he returned their greeting by gesture. And this hadith was reported by other than Nabil from Ibn Umar from Bilal, while Nabil said: from Ibn Umar from Suhayb; none reported from Nabil except Bukayr."
"2093","Said ibn al-Musayyib from Suhayb. 2084 - Hashim ibn al-Qasim al-Harrani and Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: I heard my father Yazid ibn Sinan narrating from Ata ibn Abi Rabah who said: I heard Mujahid say: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyib say: I heard Suhayb say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: He has not believed in the Quran who permits its prohibitions. And we do not know anyone who reported these words from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Suhayb, and we do not know it reported from Suhayb except through these two chains we mentioned."
"2094","2085 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Hudhayfah narrated to me, he said: my father narrated to me, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Suhayb who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was shown your place of migration, a salty land between two lava fields; it will be either Hajar or Yathrib. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Madinah and Abu Bakr went out with him, and I had intended to go out with him. And we do not know any path for this hadith from Suhayb except this path."
"2095","Aslam, freedman of Umar, from Suhayb. 2086 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Suhayb: I love you were it not for traits in you. He said: What are they? He said: Your kunyah Abu Yahya though you have no child, and your claiming descent from al-Namir ibn Qasit though you are not of them. Suhayb said: As for my kunyah Abu Yahya, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me that kunyah and I will never leave it; as for your saying I claim descent from al-Namir ibn Qasit though I am not of them, I am of al-Namir ibn Qasit, and even if I were not of them I would not have claimed it; as for my foreign accent, I was nursed at al-Ubullah so the foreignness in my tongue is from that. Hammad ibn Salamah reported two hadiths from Zayd ibn Aslam, this is one and the other is a non-musnad hadith from Umar about the story of al-Mughirah ibn Shubah; we do not know that Aslam reported from Suhayb anything but this hadith."
"2096","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Suhayb. 2087 - Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he recited: For those who do good is the best and more. He said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise they will be called: O people of Paradise, you have an appointment not yet given to you. They will say: Did He not whiten our faces and admit us to Paradise? It will be said to them: You have an appointment not yet given to you. They will say the same, then their Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will manifest Himself to them; that is His saying: No darkness nor humiliation will cover their faces. He said: He promises the gaze at their Lord's Face, Blessed and Exalted. And this hadith was reported by Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, Hammad ibn Zayd, and Mamar, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla; Hammad said: from Thabit from Abd al-Rahman from Suhayb. When a trustworthy narrator reports a hadith, the addition belongs to him; Hammad ibn Salamah was among the best and most trustworthy people."
"2097","2088 - Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hakim ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in one of the two evening prayers, either Zuhr or Asr; when he gave salutations he turned to us smiling and said: Will you not ask me why I laughed? The people said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: I marvel at Allah's decree for the Muslim servant; all of Allah's decree for him is good, and no one for whom Allah decrees good has it good except the Muslim servant. And we do not know anyone who reported it from Yunus except Abd al-Hakim ibn Mansur al-Wasiti; Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah reported it from Thabit from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Suhayb."
"2098","2089 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, meaning al-Bunani, he is Thabit ibn Aslam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prayed sat and whispered, which he had not done before; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Did you notice what I do? We said: Yes. He said: I remembered a prophet who was impressed by the multitude of his people and said: These will never be overcome, or said: they will never be defeated; so it was said to him: Give your people choice of three: either I set upon them an enemy from others who destroys them, or I set hunger upon them, or I set death upon them. He informed his people of that; they said: Choose for us, for our Lord has entrusted us to you. He said: So he performed ablution and prayed - Sulayman said: they used to hasten to prayer - and said: O Lord, as to setting their enemy upon them to destroy them, no; as to setting hunger upon them, no; but death. So seventy thousand died in three days. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So my whisper which you see is my saying: O Allah, by You I move, O Allah, by You I attack, O Allah, by You I fight. Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah said: There is no power nor strength except by Allah. And we do not know anyone who reported this hadith with these words from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Suhayb, and we do not know any path from Suhayb except this path."
"2099","2090 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to me, he wrote it with his hand and read it to me, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was a king among those before you who entrusted a boy of his to a magician who taught him magic; between the magician and the king was a monk. The boy came upon the monk and heard his speech and liked his manner and speech. When he came to the magician he would say: What kept you? He would say: My family kept me; when he came to his family he sat with the monk and was late, and when he came to his family they beat him. He complained to the monk, who said: When the magician wants to beat you say: my family kept me; when your family wants to beat you say: the magician kept me. While thus, one day he came upon a terrible huge beast that had blocked the people so they could not pass. He said: Today I will know whether the monk is more beloved to Allah or the magician. He said: O Allah, if the monk's affair is more beloved - more pleasing - to You than the magician's, kill this beast so people may pass. He threw at it and killed it, and the people went on. He informed the monk of that, who said: You are better than me; you will be tested, and if tested do not point to me. The boy used to cure the blind and the leper. There was a companion of the king, a man who sat with him, who became blind; he heard of him - meaning the boy - and came to him with many gifts and said: Heal me. He said: I do not heal anyone; if you believe in Allah I will call upon Allah and He will heal you. He believed, he called upon Allah and He healed him. Then he came to the king - meaning the man he used to visit - and sat as before. The king said to him: Who returned your sight? He said: My Lord. He said: I am your lord? He said: No, but my Lord is Allah. He said: Do you have a lord besides me? He said: Yes. He kept torturing him until he pointed to the boy; he sent for him and said: Your magic has reached healing the blind and leper? He said: I do not heal anyone; none heals but Allah. He said: Do you have a lord besides me? He said: Yes, my Lord and your Lord is Allah. He seized him too with torture until he pointed to the monk; the monk was brought and told: Return from your religion, but he refused, so a saw was placed on the parting of his head until its halves fell to the ground. He said to the blind man: Return from your religion, but he refused, so a saw was placed on the parting of his head until its halves fell to the ground. He said to the boy: Return from your religion, but he refused, so he sent him with men to such-and-such mountain and said: When you reach it with him, if he returns from his religion, else hurl him from it. They took him up the mountain and he said: O Allah, suffice me against them however You will; the mountain shook with them. The boy came walking to the king, who said: What happened to your companions? He said: Allah sufficed me against them. He sent him with others to the sea and said: If he returns from his religion, else drown him; they took him out to sea, and the boy said: O Allah, suffice me against them however You will; they all drowned. The boy came walking to the king, who said: What happened to your companions? He said: Allah sufficed me against them. Then he said to the king: You cannot kill me until you do what I command; if you do what I command you will kill me, else you cannot kill me. He said: What is it? He said: Gather the people on one plain, crucify me on a trunk, take an arrow from my quiver, then say: In the name of Allah, Lord of the boy; if you do that you will kill me. He said: He placed the arrow in the bow's notch, shot it and said: In the name of Allah, Lord of the boy; the arrow fell on his temple, the boy placed his hand on the arrow's spot and died. The people said: We believe in the Lord of the boy. It was said to the king: What you feared has, by Allah, befallen you; all the people have believed. He ordered the mouths of the roads, trenches were dug there and fires kindled, and said: Whoever returns from his religion leave him, else hurl him in. They were falling into it; a woman came with her nursing infant and seemed to hesitate to fall in, so the infant said to her: O mother, be patient, for you are upon the truth."
"2100","2091 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sanani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. And we do not know anyone who reports these words from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Suhayb, and we do not know anyone who reported it except Thabit from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Suhayb."
"2101","Kab al-Ahbar from Suhayb. 2092 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ata ibn Abi Marwan, from his father, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Mughith al-Aslami narrated to him, he said: Kab said: We find in the Torah that Dawud, Prophet of Allah, when he finished his prayer would say: O Allah, set right for me my religion which You made the safeguard of my affair, and set right for me my world in which You placed my livelihood. O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, in Your pardon from Your punishment, and in You from You; none withholds what You give, none gives what You withhold, and the wealth of the wealthy does not avail him against You. Kab al-Ahbar said: Suhayb the good informed that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to finish his prayer with these words; that is what prompted Kab to the hadith."
"2102","2093 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ata ibn Abi Marwan, from his father who said: Kab al-Ahbar said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never came to a town intending to enter it except he said when he saw it: O Allah, Lord of the heavens and what they shade, Lord of the seven earths and what they bear, Lord of the devils and what they mislead, Lord of the winds and what they scatter; we ask You for the good of this town and the good of its people, and seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of its people, or from its evil and the evil within it. Kab said: Suhayb narrated this hadith to him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And these two hadiths we do not know reported from Suhayb except through this chain with this isnad."
"2103","Hamzah ibn Suhayb from his father. 2094 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Hamzah ibn Suhayb, from his father who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me the kunyah Abu Yahya. And this hadith has been reported from Suhayb through more than one chain; we do not know that Hamzah ibn Suhayb reported from his father except this hadith."
"2104","Sayfi ibn Suhayb from his father. 2095 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ziyad ibn Suhayb, from his father, from Suhayb who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and entered upon him while he was in the house of Kulthum ibn al-Hadm, with dates before them which they were eating; I had ophthalmia in one eye. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not eat dates for your eye. I said: I eat from the side of my sound eye. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his molars appeared. And we do not know anyone who reports this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Suhayb."
"2105","2096 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Salim narrated to us, he said: Abu Qudamah narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Sayfi ibn Suhayb narrated to me, that his father informed him from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Hold to black seed, for in it is healing from every disease except al-sam. They said: What is al-sam? He said: Death. Hold to ajwah dates, for they are a remedy for every poison; hold to the milk of wild camels, for it is a remedy for every disease. And we do not preserve this from Suhayb except through this chain with this isnad."
"2106","2097 - And Ziyad ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Sayfi ibn Suhayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold to black dye, for it is more fearsome for you in your enemies' hearts and more beloved by your women to you. And we do not know this hadith reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain."
"2107","2098 - And my father narrated it to me, he said: Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: al-Daffa ibn Daghfal al-Sadusi narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Sayfi ibn Suhayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"2108","2099 - And al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Mihja narrated to us, he said: al-Daffa ibn Daghfal narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Sayfi ibn Suhayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. And Ziyad ibn Ubayd Allah omitted al-Daffa ibn Daghfal in the isnad. And we do not know anyone who reported this hadith except al-Daffa, and its isnad is not strong."
"2109","2100 - And Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Dubai narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar, freedman of Al al-Zubayr, narrated to us, from Sayfi ibn Suhayb, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire. And we do not know this hadith reported from Suhayb except through this chain."
"2110","2101 - And Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Sayyar, meaning Ibn Hatim, narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Sulayman, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Suhayb, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"2111","2102 - And Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sayfi ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from his great-grandfather, from Suhayb who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him love Suhayb as a mother loves her child."
"2112","2103 - And with his isnad he said: I accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before he entered Madinah. And we do not know this hadith reported except from Suhayb with this isnad."
"2113","2104 - And Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Ghanim narrated to us, from Ibn Suhayb, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's prayer in congregation equals his prayer alone by twenty-five, meaning twenty-five prayers."
"2114","Musnad of al-Miqdad ibn Amr ibn al-Aswad, may Allah be pleased with him. Musnad of al-Miqdad ibn Amr ibn al-Aswad, kunyah Abu Mabad. Ibn Abbas from al-Miqdad. 2105 - Ishaq ibn Shahin al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Miqdad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2115","2106 - And Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Miqdad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you see those who praise excessively, throw dust in their faces. And we do not know that Ibn Abbas reported from al-Miqdad except this hadith."
"2116","Hammam ibn al-Harith from al-Miqdad. 2107 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam, from al-Miqdad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you see those who praise excessively, throw dust in their faces. And we do not know that Hammam reported from al-Miqdad except this hadith."
"2117","Yazid ibn Sharik from al-Miqdad. 2108 - Hisham ibn Yunus al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father who said: We were with Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, and a man began praising him, so al-Miqdad began throwing dust in his face, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When you see those who praise excessively, throw dust in their faces. And we do not know anyone who reported it from al-Amash with this isnad except Hafs ibn Ghiyath."
"2118","Maymun ibn Abi Shabib from al-Miqdad. 2109 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from al-Miqdad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you see those who praise excessively, throw dust in their faces. And we do not know that Maymun ibn Abi Shabib reported from al-Miqdad except this hadith."
"2119","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from al-Miqdad. 2110 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, meaning al-Bunani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Miqdad who said: I came with two companions of mine, our sight and hearing gone from hunger; we began offering ourselves to the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and none accepted us. We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he took us along; there were three goats. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Milk this milk and divide it among us. We did so and set aside for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he would come at night and greet with a greeting that did not wake the sleeper but was heard by the wakeful, then go to the mosque and pray, then come to his drink and drink. One night Satan came to me and said: Muhammad visits the Ansar who present gifts to him and gets provisions from them; he has no need of this sip. He kept at me until I drank it; when he knew I had hidden it in my belly and there was no way to it, he made me regret, saying: Woe to you, what have you done? You drank the drink of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Muhammad will come and supplicate against you and you will perish, losing your world and Hereafter. I had a shawl; when I raised it over my head my feet showed, when I let it over my feet my head showed. Sleep would not come to me, while my two companions slept and did not do what I did. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, greeted, went to the mosque, prayed, came to his drink, uncovered it and found nothing in it, and raised his head. I said: Now he will supplicate against me and I will perish. He said: O Allah, feed whoever fed me and give drink to whoever gave me drink. When I heard that I tightened my shawl and took the knife and went to the goats looking to choose the fattest to slaughter for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I felt them and they were all full of milk. I went to a vessel of Muhammad's household they had not hoped to milk into, milked into it until froth covered it, and brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Have you not drunk your drink? I said: O Messenger of Allah, drink. He drank, then handed to me. I said: Drink. He drank, then handed to me. I took what remained; when I knew the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had drunk and I was safe from his supplication, I laughed till I fell to the ground. He said: One of your misdeeds, O Miqdad? I said: O Messenger of Allah, such-and-such happened; I told him what I had done. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This was only mercy from Allah; why did you not inform me so we could wake your two companions? I said: By Him who sent you with the truth, I do not care once you have had some of it and I have had some of it, whoever among people has had. And we do not know these words reported with this wording except from al-Miqdad alone, and we do not know any isnad from al-Miqdad except this isnad."
"2120","Ubayd Allah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar from al-Miqdad. 2111 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Minqari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Kabir ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Ubayd Allah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar, from al-Miqdad ibn Amr al-Kindi - he was among those who witnessed Badr - that he informed him he said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a man I meet who fights me and cuts off one of my hands, then takes shelter from me by a tree and says: I submit to Allah; shall I kill him, O Messenger of Allah? He said: If you kill him he is in your position before you fought him, and you are in his position before he said the words he said. And we do not know this hadith reported from al-Miqdad except with this isnad; more than one reported it from al-Zuhri so we sufficed with Abd al-Hamid."
"2121","Jubayr ibn Nufayr from al-Miqdad. 2112 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father who said: al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad came for a need, so we said: Sit till we seek your need for you. He sat and said: I marvel at people I passed by who wish for tribulations, claiming Allah will test them therein as He tested His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions, may Allah be pleased with them. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The fortunate is he who is kept away from tribulations; the fortunate is he who is kept away from tribulations - repeating it three times - except one who is tested and endures. By Allah, I will not testify for anyone that he is among the people of Paradise until I know upon what he dies, after a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The heart of the son of Adam turns over more violently than a pot when it boils. And we do not preserve these words except from al-Miqdad from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except a man who reversed it making it from al-Miqdam; in our view the correct is al-Miqdad, and its isnad is a hasan isnad."
"2122","Abu Mamar from al-Miqdad. 2113 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Mujahid, from Abu Mamar, from al-Miqdad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you see those who praise excessively, throw dust in their faces. And this hadith was reported by al-Thawri and Qays from Habib from Mujahid from Abu Mamar from al-Miqdad."
"2123","2114 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Mukhawwal ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Mujahid, from Abu Mamar, from al-Miqdad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2124","Abu Taybah al-Kalai from al-Miqdad. 2115 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sad al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Taybah al-Kalai say: I heard al-Miqdad ibn Amr ibn al-Aswad say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: What do you say about adultery? They said: Forbidden, Allah and His Messenger forbade it, so it is forbidden till the Day of Resurrection. He said: For a man to commit adultery with ten women is easier for him than to commit adultery with his neighbor's wife. What do you say about theft? They said: Forbidden, Allah and His Messenger forbade it, so it is forbidden till the Day of Resurrection. He said: For a man to steal from ten houses is easier for him than to steal from his neighbor's house. And we do not preserve anyone who reported this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except al-Miqdad."
"2125","Dubaa bint al-Zubayr from al-Miqdad. 2116 - Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Yaqub narrated to us, he said: my aunt Quraybah bint Abd Allah narrated to me, from her mother Karimah bint al-Miqdad ibn Amr, from Dubaa bint al-Zubayr, she was under al-Miqdad ibn Amr, she said: People used to go only every two or three days and defecate as camels defecate; one day al-Miqdad went out for his need till he came to al-Baqi, the Baqi of al-Gharqad, and entered a ruin for his need. While sitting, a rat came out of a hole bringing out a dinar, and kept bringing out dinar after dinar till it brought out seventeen dinars, then brought out the edge of a rag. al-Miqdad said: So I stood and took it and found in it a dinar, totaling eighteen dinars. I brought them to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of it. He said: Did you follow your hand into the hole? I said: No, by Him who sent you with the truth. He said: There is no charity in it; may Allah bless it for you. Before the last of it was spent, I saw sacks of silver in al-Miqdad's house. And we do not know anyone who reported these words from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except al-Miqdad, and we do not know any path from al-Miqdad except this path. This Musa ibn Yaqub is a well-known man of Madinah; this Quraybah is bint Abd Allah ibn Wahb ibn Zamah; Karimah bint al-Miqdad, we do not know anyone who reported from her except Quraybah bint Abd Allah."
"2126","2117 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athmah narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Yaqub narrated to us, he said: my aunt Quraybah bint Abd Allah narrated to me, from her mother Karimah bint al-Miqdad, from Dubaa bint al-Zubayr, from al-Miqdad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hope for them - meaning his wives - the truthful. We said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the truthful; are they the children who perish while young? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The truthful are those who give charity. And we do not know anyone who reported these words from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except al-Miqdad, and we do not know any path from him except this path."
"2127","2118 - Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Jabbar ibn Said al-Musahiqi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Yaqub narrated to me, he said: my aunt Quraybah bint Abd Allah narrated to me, from her mother Karimah, from Dubaa bint al-Zubayr, from al-Miqdad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the horse two shares and its rider one share. And we do not know this hadith reported from al-Miqdad except with this isnad."
"2128","Musnad of Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, may Allah be pleased with him. Musnad of Khabbab ibn al-Aratt from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Anas ibn Malik from Khabbab. 2119 - Abd Allah ibn Jafar al-Barmaki narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from Khabbab ibn al-Aratt who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, strengthen Islam with the more beloved of the two men to You: Umar ibn al-Khattab or Abu Jahl ibn Hisham. And we do not know that Anas ibn Malik reported from Khabbab except this hadith, nor any isnad from Anas except this isnad."
"2129","Abu Umamah from Khabbab. 2120 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zuhr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from Khabbab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning; they are those who do not use cautery nor seek ruqyah - I think he said - nor take omens, and upon their Lord they rely."
"2130","2121 - And Umar ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from Khabbab who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The believer is rewarded for everything except building in this dust."
"2131","Abd Allah ibn Khabbab from his father Khabbab. 2122 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Abd Allah ibn Khabbab, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer and lengthened it; it was said to him: You lengthened it. He said: I prayed a prayer of hope and fear; I asked my Lord therein three things, He gave me two and withheld one: I asked Him not to punish them with a punishment by which He destroyed those before them, and He gave it to me; I asked Him not to set over them an enemy who destroys them, and He gave it to me; I asked Him not to divide them into factions making them taste one another's might, and He withheld it from me. And we do not know this hadith reported from Khabbab except with this isnad."
"2132","2123 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Abu Yunus, his name Hatim ibn Abi Sagheirah, narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd Allah ibn Khabbab, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers over you who lie and oppress; whoever rejects has cleared himself, whoever hates has been safe, but whoever is pleased and follows. They said: Shall we not kill them? He said: No, so long as they establish prayer. And we do not know any path for this hadith from Khabbab except this path."
"2133","Masruq ibn al-Ajda from Khabbab. 2124 - Rizq Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Duha narrated to us, from Masruq, from Khabbab who said: I was a blacksmith and I had a debt upon al-As ibn Wail; I came to him demanding it. He said: I will not pay you till you disbelieve in Muhammad. I said: I will not disbelieve in him till you die, then live, then die. He said: So you claim I will live; there I will have wealth and children and will pay you. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: Have you seen him who disbelieved in Our verses and said: I will surely be given wealth and children; did he look into the unseen or take a covenant with the Most Merciful; no, We will write what he says and extend for him punishment extensively; and We will inherit from him what he says and he will come to Us alone. And we do not know that Masruq reported from Khabbab except this hadith."
"2134","Qays ibn Abi Hazim from Khabbab. 2125 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ismail, from Qays who said: We entered upon Khabbab when he had been cauterized, and he said: Were it not that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to supplicate for death, I would have supplicated for it. He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The believer is rewarded for everything except building in this dust. And we do not know anyone who raised it all from the first to last from Ismail from Qays except Abu Muawiyah; more than one reported the beginning of the hadith from Ismail from Qays from Khabbab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to supplicate for death; as for that the believer is rewarded for everything except building in this dust, we know no one who combined it except Abu Muawiyah."
"2135","2126 - Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Uqayli, Ahmad ibn Abdah, and Abd al-Ala ibn Zayd narrated to us, all narrated to us from Sufyan, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid and Bayan, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Khabbab who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he sat at the Kabah resting on his cloak, and he said: You will be victorious. And he said: Among those before you, one would be combed with iron combs beneath the bone of flesh, yet that did not turn him from his religion."
"2136","2127 - And Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah al-Yashkuri, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Khabbab who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he sat at the Kabah resting on his cloak, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among those before you, one would be combed with iron combs beneath the bone of flesh, yet that did not turn him from his religion. And we do not know any path for this hadith from Khabbab except these two paths. As for the hadith of al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah, we know none who reported it except Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi from Yahya ibn Salamah from his father; we do not know that Salamah reported from al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah except this hadith, nor that anyone reported the hadith of Bayan from Qays from Khabbab except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, for he combined Ismail and Bayan."
"2137","2128 - And al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Sukayn narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Ismail narrated to us, from Qays, from Khabbab who said: I used to make the spear for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Bakr said: Khabbab's saying: I used to make the spear for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), means the short spear among those about which it was reported that he would pray toward it like a staff. And we do not know anyone who reported it from Ismail from Qays from Khabbab except Yazid ibn Ata and Amr ibn al-Nadr."
"2138","Abu al-Kanud from Khabbab. 2129 - al-Husayn ibn Amr al-Anqazi narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abu Sad, from Abu al-Kanud, from Khabbab."
"2139","2130 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abu Sad al-Azdi, from Abu al-Kanud, from Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, regarding the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening seeking His Face. He said: Uyaynah ibn Hisn and al-Aqra ibn Habis came and found the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting with Bilal, Ammar, Suhayb and Khabbab ibn al-Aratt among weak believers. When they saw them around him they despised them, came to him privately and said: We would like you to allot us a share from you by which the Arabs know us, for Arab delegations come to you, and we are ashamed that the Arabs see us with these slaves; when we come to you, stand them up, and when we finish, seat them if you wish. He said: Yes. They said: Write us a document. He called for a sheet to write for them and called Ali to write for them, while we sat in a corner, when Jibril came down with this verse: And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening seeking His Face; nothing of their account is upon you nor anything of your account upon them, lest you drive them away and be among the wrongdoers; then he mentioned al-Aqra and his companion, saying: Thus We tried some of them with others that they say: Are these whom Allah favored among us; is not Allah most knowing of the grateful; then he mentioned, saying: When those who believe in Our verses come to you, say: Peace be upon you; your Lord has prescribed mercy upon Himself, that whoever of you does evil; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw the sheet aside, and I do not forget him saying: Peace be upon you. We drew near him that day till we placed our knees upon his knees. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sit with us before that, and when he wished to rise he rose and left us; so Allah revealed: And keep yourself with those who call upon their Lord morning and evening seeking His Face, and let not your eyes pass beyond them desiring the adornment of worldly life - meaning the gatherings of nobles - and obey not one whose heart We made heedless of Our remembrance and who follows his desire and whose affair is waste; as for one whose heart We made heedless, it is Uyaynah and al-Aqra ibn Habis; as for waste, it is ruin. Then he struck for them the parable of two men and the parable of worldly life. He said: We used to sit with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when we reached the hour in which he used to rise, we rose and left him till he rose whenever he rose. And we do not know anyone who reported this hadith with these words except Khabbab, and we do not know any path from Khabbab except this path."
"2140","Abu Mamar from Khabbab. 2131 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar who said: We said to Khabbab: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite anything in the daytime prayer? He said: Yes. We said: How did you know that? He said: By the movement of his beard. And we do not know any path for this hadith from Khabbab except this path, and we do not know that Abu Mamar reported from Khabbab except this hadith."
"2141","Abu Wail from Khabbab. 2132 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Khabbab who said: We migrated to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and our reward fell upon Allah; among us are those who hastened, and among us are those whose fruit ripened and he gathers it. And we do not know that Abu Wail reported from Khabbab except this hadith."
"2142","Amr ibn Shurahbil from Khabbab. 2133 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Fitr, meaning Ibn Khalifah, narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Shurahbil who said: I entered upon Khabbab in his illness and he said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None of you should wish for death - I would have wished for it. And we do not know that Amr ibn Shurahbil reported from Khabbab except this hadith."
"2143","Said ibn Wahb from Khabbab. 2134 - al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi Abd al-Kabir ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Wahb, from Khabbab who said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the heat of the ground and he did not relieve us; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Zuhr at midday heat. And we do not know that Said ibn Wahb reported from Khabbab except this hadith."
"2144","Harithah ibn Mudarrib from Khabbab. 2135 - Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad Abu Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Khabbab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should wish for death. And we do not know this hadith reported from al-Amash except from Abu Shihab."
"2145","2136 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from some of his companions, from Khabbab who said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the heat of the ground and he did not relieve us."
"2146","The elders from Khabbab. 2137 - Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Kaysan Abu Umar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Bilal, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you fast, use the tooth-stick in the morning and do not use it in the evening, for when the fasting person's lips dry he will have light on the Day of Resurrection."
"2147","2138 - Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Kaysan Abu Umar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Bilal, from Khabbab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. And we do not know these words reported from Khabbab from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain with this isnad."
"2148","2139 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Rabi ibn Tariq narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from Khabbab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning; they are those who do not use cautery nor seek ruqyah - I think he said - nor take omens, and upon their Lord they rely. He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The believer is rewarded for everything except building in this dust. And we do not know that Abu Umamah reported from Khabbab except these two hadiths."
"2149","The daughter of Khabbab from her father. 2140 - Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Mukhawwal ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman, from the daughter of Khabbab who said: My father went out on a campaign leaving us only a ewe; he said to us: When you wish to milk it, bring it to the people of the Suffah. I went with it and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he took it and held it - or clasped it - and milked a full cup, then said: Go and bring me the largest vessel you have. I found nothing but the kneading bowl - I think she said: so he milked till he filled it - then said: Go, drink and give your neighbors to drink; when you wish to milk it, bring it to me. We prospered till my father came; my father took it and held and clasped it, and it returned to its former milk. My mother said to him: You spoiled our ewe; it used to milk a full bowl. He said: Who used to milk it? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Do you want from me the blessing of the Messenger of Allah's hand; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is of greater blessing than my hands."
"2150","2141 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Yusuf ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mudrik al-Akhmasi, from the daughter of Khabbab, from Khabbab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"2151","Musnad of al-Fadl ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him. Musnad of al-Fadl ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ibn Abbas from al-Fadl; Ali ibn al-Husayn from Ibn Abbas. 2142 - Abu Bakr ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas who said: I was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he kept saying the talbiyah till he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah, stoning it with seven pebbles, saying takbir with each pebble. And this hadith from al-Fadl from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he stoned the jamrah with seven pebbles saying takbir with each, we know none who reported it except Ali ibn al-Husayn from Ibn Abbas from al-Fadl; we know none who narrated it from Jafar except Hafs ibn Ghiyath."
"2152","Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from al-Fadl ibn Abbas. 2143 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that he said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Muzdalifah while a bedouin traveled beside him with a beautiful daughter of his whom he had mounted behind him; I began looking at her, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began turning my face away from her. He did not stop the talbiyah till he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah. And we do not know that Abu Ishaq reported from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas from al-Fadl except this hadith."
"2153","2144 - And Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim and Khusayf, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He kept saying the talbiyah till he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"2154","Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Ibn Abbas from al-Fadl ibn Abbas. 2145 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying the talbiyah till he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"2155","2146 - And Jamil ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, he said: Said, meaning Ibn Abi Arubah, narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas who said: I was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Sacrifice from Jam, and he kept saying the talbiyah till he stoned the farthest jamrah. And we do not know anyone who reported it from Said ibn Abi Arubah with this isnad except Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan; Ibrahim ibn Tahman corroborated him, and the preserved is from Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan."
"2156","2147 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Jabir, Amir al-Ahwal and Ibn Ata, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl, that he was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and would say the talbiyah on the Day of Sacrifice till he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah. And we know no one who combined Jabir, Amir and Ibn Ata from Ata from Ibn Abbas in this hadith except Shubah."
"2157","2148 - And Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Maslamah informed us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying the talbiyah till he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah. And this hadith contains discussion from Usamah ibn Zayd about entering the House, so we abridged from it what was from al-Fadl."
"2158","2149 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, meaning Ibn Artah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he kept saying the talbiyah on the Day of Sacrifice till he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"2159","2150 - And Ali ibn Shuayb narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, he said: Said, meaning Ibn Abi Arubah, narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Shinzhir, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas who said: I was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Sacrifice from Jam, and he kept saying the talbiyah till he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah. And we do not know anyone who reported it from Kathir ibn Shinzhir from Ata from Ibn Abbas from al-Fadl except Said ibn Abi Arubah."
"2160","2151 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibn Abi Najih and Aban ibn Salih, from Mujahid and Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: My brother al-Fadl ibn Abbas narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the talbiyah till he reached Jamrat al-Aqabah. And we do not know anyone who reported it from Ibn Abi Najih nor from Aban ibn Salih except Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"2161","2152 - Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Rabah ibn Abi Maruf narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the talbiyah till he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"2162","2153 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mushash, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the weak of Banu Hashim and their children to depart from Jam by night, saying: O sons, or little sons, do not stone the jamrah till the sun rises. And we do not preserve this from Mushash Abu al-Azhar except from Shubah from him."
"2163","2154 - Humayd ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Man ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt, from his father, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them in his illness in which he died; he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, my departure from among you has drawn near; whoever I have reviled in honor, here is my honor; whoever I have struck in back, here is my back, let him retaliate. Then he said: Truth after me is with Umar wherever he is. And we do not know this hadith reported from al-Fadl from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this isnad."
"2164","2155 - And Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three garments. And this hadith was reported from Ata by Ibn Abi Layla and Yaqub ibn Ata; we know no path from al-Fadl except those we named."
"2165","Mujahid from Ibn Abbas from al-Fadl. 2156 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Najih and Aban ibn Salih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas who said: My brother al-Fadl narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the talbiyah till he reached Jamrat al-Aqabah, and when he stoned it he stopped."
"2166","2157 - And Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim and Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the talbiyah till he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"2167","2158 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, he is Ibn Abi Dhubab, narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying the talbiyah till he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice. And we do not know that al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman reported from Mujahid from Ibn Abbas from al-Fadl except this hadith."
"2168","2159 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl, similarly."
"2169","Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas from al-Fadl ibn Abbas. 2160 - Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) exhorted the people in the two rakahs after Fajr before the Subh prayer; he exhorted them, then raised his voice and said: Pray before Subh even one rakah; after that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw them praying them along with the iqamah of prayer, and said again: Will you desist; two prayers together? And we do not know this hadith reported from al-Fadl except through this chain with this isnad."
"2170","2161 - And Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi informed us, he said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from al-Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing at Arafah stretching his hands like a beggar, or a word like it. And we do not know any path for this hadith from al-Fadl except this path."
"2171","Abu Mabad from Ibn Abbas from al-Fadl ibn Abbas. 2162 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj who said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, from Abu Mabad, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the people on the evening of Arafah and morning of Jam when they moved on, while holding back his camel: Hold to calmness, till he entered Mina; when he descended Muhassir he said: Hold to pebbles of khadhf with which the jamrah is stoned; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured with his hand as a man throws pebbles."
"2172","2163 - Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from his brother, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, that Abu al-Zubayr informed him that Abu Mabad narrated from Ibn Abbas from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that he narrated to him, he said: When it was the Day of Arafah and he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Ibn Abbas said - people were many around the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when people crowded upon him I said: al-Fadl will inform me of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did. al-Fadl said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) moved on with the people, pulling his camel's head and restraining it, calling: O people, calmness; till he came to Muzdalifah and prayed Maghrib and Isha, then spent the night at Muzdalifah till dawn broke and prayed Subh there, then stood at al-Mashar al-Haram; people moved on with him till he came to Muhassir and hastened through it a while, saying: Hold to pebbles like those of khadhf. And we do not know anyone who reported it from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari except Sulayman ibn Bilal."
"2173","2164 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu Mabad, from Ibn Abbas, I think from al-Fadl ibn Abbas - I found it in my book in another place from Sufyan from Ziyad ibn Sad from Abu al-Zubayr from Abu Mabad from Ibn Abbas, and I did not see in it from al-Fadl - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Move away from Muhassir."
"2174","Yusuf ibn Mihran from Ibn Abbas from al-Fadl ibn Abbas. 2165 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the talbiyah till he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah. And we do not know that Yusuf ibn Mihran reported from Ibn Abbas from al-Fadl except this hadith."
"2175","Abu Hurayrah from al-Fadl. 2166 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Abu Hurayrah used to say: Whoever wakes junub in Ramadan has no fast; Marwan sent to Umm Salamah asking her about that. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake junub in Ramadan, then bathe and fast. He sent that to Abu Hurayrah, who said: al-Fadl ibn Abbas only narrated it to me. And we do not know that Abu Hurayrah reported from al-Fadl except this hadith."
"2176","Abu al-Tufayl from al-Fadl 2167 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued the talbiya on the Day of Sacrifice until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqaba. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Wuhayb, from Ibn Khuthaym."
"2177","Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman from al-Fadl 2168 - Safwan ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Waqid narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman, from his father, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prayed the two rak'as of Fajr would lie down on his right side. And we do not know this hadith narrated from al-Fadl except through this route, and we do not know Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman narrated from al-Fadl anything except this hadith."
"2178","Rabi'a ibn al-Harith from al-Fadl 2169 - Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Sa'id, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Abd Allah ibn Nafi' ibn al-Amya, from Rabi'a ibn al-Harith, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Prayer is two by two; you make tashahhud in every rak'a, then you supplicate humbly and submissively and lowly, then you raise your hands to your ears, then you turn them toward your face and say: O Lord, O Lord; whoever does not do that, it is deficient (khidaj)."" Thus Ibrahim said, and it is in fact: you raise your hands to your two thanudwas (upper chest). And we do not know Rabi'a ibn al-Harith narrated from al-Fadl except this hadith."
"2179","Musnad Aqil ibn Abi Talib from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Musa ibn Talha from Aqil 2170 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Talha ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Musa ibn Talha: Aqil ibn Abi Talib narrated to me, he said: Quraysh came to Abu Talib and said: your nephew harms us in our gathering place and our mosque, so forbid him from harming us. He said: O Aqil, go to Muhammad and call him. So I went and brought him; he came in the middle of the day walking through the shade, and sat at the threshold of the door while Quraysh were with Abu Talib. He said: O son of my brother, your cousins claim you harm them in their gathering and mosque, so refrain from that. He said: then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his gaze to the sky, then said: ""Do you see this sun?"" They said: yes. He said: ""I am no more able to abandon that than you are to kindle a flame from it for me."" He said: so Abu Talib said: the son of my brother has not lied to us, so go back. He said: so they went back. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Aqil except through this route with this chain."
"2180","Muhammad ibn Aqil from his father 2171 - Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us: Bukayr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban al-Anazi narrated to us: Mindal, meaning Ibn Ali, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from his father, from his grandfather Aqil ibn Abi Talib: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with a sa'. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Aqil except through this route. And Mindal erred in this hadith when he gave it this chain; rather Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated it from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah."
"2181","Al-Hasan from Aqil 2172 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Yunus, meaning Ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan: that Aqil ibn Abi Talib married a woman from Banu Hashim, and the people came to him and said: ""Will you not let us congratulate you?"" And they began saying: with harmony and sons (bir-rifa' wal-banin). So he said: do not say that; rather say: may Allah bless for you, may He bless upon you; we were commanded with that. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from al-Hasan, from Aqil, and I do not think al-Hasan heard from Aqil."
"2182","Musnad Nawfal ibn al-Harith, may Allah be pleased with him; Musnad Nawfal ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) 2173 - Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book in his handwriting, from Sa'id ibn Sulayman ibn Sa'id ibn Nawfal ibn al-Harith, from his father, from his grandfather, from Nawfal ibn al-Harith, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about prayer in sheep pens. He said: ""Pray in their resting places and wipe their nasal filth, for they are among the beasts of Paradise."" And we do not know Nawfal ibn al-Harith narrated anything except this hadith, and we do not know for it any route except this route."
"2183","Musnad Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) 2174 - Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, the nephew of al-Zuhri, narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to me at al-Rusafa, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib, he said: the last prayer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us was Maghrib; he recited in the first rak'a ""Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,"" and in the second ""Say: O you disbelievers."" And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except through this route, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri except al-Hajjaj ibn Nusayr."
"2184","Musnad al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'a 2175 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us: Jarir, meaning Ibn Abd al-Hamid, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'a, he said: al-Abbas came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while angry, and he said: ""What is the matter with you?"" He said: O Messenger of Allah, when we go out we see Quraysh talking, and when they see us they fall silent. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, faith does not enter a man's heart until he loves you for Allah and for my kinship."""
"2185","2176 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'a, he said: al-Abbas stood up to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while angry and said: ""What is the matter with you?"" He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the matter between us and Quraysh? He said: ""What is the matter between you and them?"" He said: they meet one another with radiant faces, but when they meet us they meet us with otherwise. So he became angry until a vein between his eyes swelled, then he said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, faith does not enter a man's heart until he loves you for Allah and for His Messenger."" Then he said: ""What is the matter with men who harm me concerning al-Abbas; a man's uncle is the like of his father."" And we do not know Ibn Rabi'a narrated anything except these two hadiths; more than one narrated them from Yazid. And Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid differed from Yazid in the first one, saying: from Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas; while Yazid narrates it from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'a. Thus Jarir and others narrated it; and Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated it from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas. And we do not judge either of them to be more established and sound in hadith than his companion, except that Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad is not strong in hadith, nor firmly established such that his solitary narration is used as proof according to the people of knowledge of transmission. End of the twentieth part, and praise be to Allah abundantly as He deserves."
"2186","Musnad Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with them both; first of the Musnad of Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Abida ibn Amr al-Salmani from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr 2177 - Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib ibn Yahya al-Raqqi al-Sammut informed us, he said: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abida ibn Amr al-Salmani, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: that two men laid claim against each other before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the one claimed against swore by Allah besides Whom there is no god. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah has forgiven you by your sincerity."""
"2187","2178 - And Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn ibn Kurdi narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abida, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. And no one followed Shu'ba in this narration of his from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib; they differed with him in it: Hammad ibn Salama and Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid said: from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Yahya, from Ibn Abbas: that two men disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And I do not think this discrepancy came except from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, for he had become confused in his hadith. And Abida did not narrate from Ibn al-Zubayr any supported (musnad) hadith except this hadith through a sound route. He said: and I heard Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna saying: I copied this hadith from the book of Ghundar, from Shu'ba, from Ata, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abida, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I did not hear it from him."
"2188","Urwa ibn al-Zubayr from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr 2179 - Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every prophet has a disciple (hawari), and my disciple is al-Zubayr."" And this hadith has been narrated from Hisham through various routes, and they differed over Hisham: Abu Mu'awiya said: from Hisham, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Ibn al-Zubayr; and more than one said: from Hisham, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir. And we do not know anyone who said: from Hisham, from his father, except Hammad ibn Zayd."
"2189","2180 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""One suck nor two sucks do not prohibit (marriage)."" And this hadith was narrated by the memorizers (huffaz) from Hisham, from his father, from Ibn al-Zubayr; and al-Zuhri narrated it from Urwa, from A'isha and Ibn al-Zubayr. And a man who is not a memorizer, called Muhammad ibn Dinar, narrated it from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from his father."
"2190","2181 - Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Uqayli narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: when this verse was revealed, ""Take pardoning,"" the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to take pardoning from people's conduct. And this hadith is only narrated from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father; and we do not know anyone who said ""from Ibn al-Zubayr"" except Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"2191","2182 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, and it is the correct one."
"2192","2183 - Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, or Umar ibn Ali, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: this verse was revealed, ""And when they hear what was sent down to the Messenger you see their eyes overflow with tears."" He said: it was revealed concerning al-Najashi and his companions. And this hadith, even though it mentions no speech from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in it, yet it says ""was revealed,"" and it was only revealed upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2193","2184 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us: Hafs ibn Maysara narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Al-umra (a life grant of property) is permissible for its recipients."" And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith from Hisham, from his father, from Ibn al-Zubayr except Hafs ibn Maysara; and others besides Hafs narrate it from Hisham, from his father, as mursal."
"2194","2185 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan narrated to us: Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Abu Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: ""My front tooth fell out (nadarut), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to take a front tooth of gold."" And some of Hisham's companions narrated this hadith from Hisham, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayy; and we do not know anyone who said ""from Ibn al-Zubayr"" except through this route."
"2195","Al-Bahiyy from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr 2186 - al-Hasan ibn Qaza'a narrated to us: Ali ibn Abis narrated to us: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Bahiyy, he said: I said to Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: inform me of the person most resembling the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: ""Al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was the person most resembling the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the most beloved of them to him. He would come while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was prostrating and fall upon his back, and he would not rise until he moved away; and he would come and enter under his belly and he would spread his legs for him until he came out."" And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except from Ibn al-Zubayr, and we do not know anyone narrated this hadith except Ali ibn Abis, from Yazid, from al-Bahiyy."
"2196","Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulayka from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr 2187 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari and Muhammad ibn Hasan ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, they said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka: that Ibn al-Zubayr narrated to them, he said: a party from Banu Tamim came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: appoint al-Qa'qa' ibn Ma'bad; and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: appoint al-Aqra' ibn Habis. Abu Bakr said: you only intended to oppose me; Umar said: I did not intend to oppose you. So they argued, and then was revealed, ""Do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet."" And we do not know this account narrated except from Ibn al-Zubayr; and Ibn Jurayj and Nafi' ibn Umar narrated it from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Ibn al-Zubayr. As for the hadith of Ibn Jurayj, we do not know anyone narrated it except al-Hajjaj ibn Muhammad."
"2197","2188 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal narrated to us: Nafi' ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Ibn al-Zubayr: that Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, when a group from Banu Tamim came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one of them pointed to al-Aqra' ibn Habis and the other pointed to another; and Abu Bakr said to Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: you only intended to oppose me. Umar said: I did not intend to oppose you. So their voices rose before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and then was revealed, ""O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet."" Ibn Abi Mulayka said: Ibn al-Zubayr said: so Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, after that, when he spoke to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), would speak to him like one confiding a secret (ka-akhi al-sirar)."
"2198","2189 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us: Nafi' ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, and he mentioned the story. Ibn Abi Mulayka said: Ibn al-Zubayr said: so Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, after that, when he spoke to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), would speak to him like one confiding a secret; he would not make him hear until he asked him to repeat."
"2199","2190 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr said: as for the one about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Had I taken a close friend (khalil) I would have taken him as a close friend"" - meaning Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him - he ruled that the grandfather is a father. And this statement has been narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr through more than one route."
"2200","2191 - Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Ata ibn al-Agharr and Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Jubayri narrated to us, they said: Nafi' ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites the Qur'an aloud or by looking, Allah will give him a tree in Paradise; if a crow hatched its young in a branch of its branches then flew, old age would overtake it before it crossed its leaves."" And we do not know this hadith narrated except from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated it from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Ibn al-Zubayr, thus following Nafi' ibn Umar."
"2201","2192 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mahan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Nafi' ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He is not of us who does not chant the Qur'an (yataghanna bil-Qur'an)."" And this hadith was disputed over from Ibn Abi Mulayka: Amr ibn Dinar and al-Layth said: from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Ibn Abi Nuhayk, from Sa'd; and Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward said: from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Ibn Abi Yazid, from Abu Lubaba; and Isl ibn Sufyan said: from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from A'isha; and Ubayd Allah ibn al-Akhnas said: from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Ibn Abbas."
"2202","2193 - Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, is but a part of me; what angers her angers me."" And on another occasion he said: ""and what harms her harms me."" And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith from Ayyub with this chain except Isma'il Ibn Ullayya. And al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated it, saying: from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from al-Miswar ibn Makhrama."
"2203","Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr 2194 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Furat al-Qazzaz, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: I was with Abd Allah ibn Utba when a letter came to him from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Had I taken a close friend or minister I would have taken Ibn Abi Quhafa as a close friend, but he is my brother in religion and my companion in the cave."" And more than one narrated this hadith from al-Hajjaj with this chain; and we do not know Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr anything except this hadith."
"2204","Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr 2195 - Zurayq ibn al-Sakht narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Salama, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""One consulted is entrusted (al-mustashar mu'taman)."" And we do not know anyone who followed Ibn Ishaq in this narration; and they differed over Abd al-Malik: more than one narrated it from Abu Awana, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Salama, as mursal; and Shayban narrated it from Abd al-Malik, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra; and Abd al-Hakim ibn Mansur narrated it from Abd al-Malik, from Abu Salama, from Abu al-Haytham ibn al-Tayyihan; and Sharik narrated it from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Salama, from Umm Salama. And Ahmad ibn Ishaq had narrated it, as I think, once from Abu Awana, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, from his father, from Ibn al-Zubayr; for I saw it with me in another place thus."
"2205","Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr 2196 - Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Habib al-Mu'allim, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn al-Zubayr: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque, for it exceeds it by a hundred."" And this hadith has been narrated from Ata, and they differed over Ata in it; and we do not know anyone who said ""for it exceeds it by a hundred"" except Ibn al-Zubayr. And Habib al-Mu'allim followed al-Rabi' ibn Subayh, narrating it from Ata, from Ibn al-Zubayr. And Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated this hadith from Ata, from Ibn Umar; and Ibn Jurayj narrated it from Ata, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra or A'isha; and Ibn Abi Layla narrated it from Ata, from Abu Hurayra."
"2206","Al-Sha'bi from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr 2197 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyayna informed us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr saying while leaning upon the Ka'ba: ""By the Lord of this House, Allah cursed al-Hakam and his offspring upon the tongue of His Prophet."" And we do not retain this statement from Ibn al-Zubayr except through this route with this chain. And Muhammad ibn Fudayl also narrated it from Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn al-Zubayr; Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated it to us with it."
"2207","Amr ibn Dinar from Ibn al-Zubayr 2198 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is closely reckoned in the account will perish."" And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr except through this route, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Amr except Muhammad ibn Muslim."
"2208","2199 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr and Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, they said: Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn al-Zubayr: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no owner of camels who does not pay their due when they come to water and in their time of need, except he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and laid flat for them on a wide flat plain; they will trample him with their hooves; whenever the first of them has passed, the last of them will be brought back upon him, until judgment is passed among the people or his way is seen."" And we do not know this hadith narrated from the hadith of Ibn al-Zubayr except with this chain, and we heard it only from the hadith of Abu Hudhayfa, from Muhammad ibn Muslim."
"2209","Wahb ibn Kaysan from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr 2200 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us: Salama ibn al-Fadl narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, he said: Abd Allah ibn Utba wrote to Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr - and he had appointed him over the judiciary of Iraq - asking him about the grandfather. So Ibn al-Zubayr wrote to him: that the one to whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Had I taken a close friend I would have taken him as a close friend,"" ruled that the grandfather is a father. And this hadith has been narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr through more than one route."
"2210","2201 - Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Ibn al-Zubayr: that he used to say at the end of his prayer when he gave salam: ""There is no god but Allah alone without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable; there is no change nor power except through Allah; we worship none but Him; to Him belong blessing, favor, and fine praise; there is no god but He, sincere to Him in religion though the polytheists dislike it."" He said: and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to proclaim Allah's greatness with them at the end of every prayer. And this hadith is only narrated from Hisham, from Abu al-Zubayr, the freedman of Ibn al-Zubayr, from Ibn al-Zubayr; and we do not know anyone narrated it from Hisham, from Wahb, from Ibn al-Zubayr, except Abu Mu'awiya."
"2211","2202 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr."" Thus Abu Mu'awiya narrated it from Hisham, from Wahb, from Ibn al-Zubayr."
"2212","2203 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Wahb ibn Kaysan: that Ibn al-Zubayr came out to them on a feast day, prayed, then gave the sermon, then said: ""This is the sunna of Allah and the sunna of His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" And this statement has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through more than one route; and this chain is among the best chains narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr."
"2213","Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr from his father 2204 - al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Rukhami narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that when he sat for the tashahhud he would fold his left leg and erect the right, place his right hand on his right thigh, point with the index finger, and make a circle. And we do not know anyone narrated it from Amr, from Amir, from his father, except al-Hajjaj, from Ibn Jurayj."
"2214","2205 - And al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub narrated it to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ziyad, meaning Ibn Sa'd, informed me, from Ibn Ajlan, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"2215","2206 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): when he sat for the tashahhud he would fold his left leg and erect the right, point with the index finger, and make a circle. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Ibn Ajlan; and Ibn Jurayj narrated it from Ziyad ibn Sa'd, from Ibn Ajlan, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And we do not know Amr ibn Dinar narrated from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, anything except this hadith; nor anyone narrated it from Amr except Ibn Jurayj, nor from Ibn Jurayj except al-Hajjaj; and no one narrated the hadith of Ibn Jurayj from Ziyad ibn Sa'd except al-Hajjaj ibn Muhammad from him."
"2216","2207 - al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly to the hadith of Ibn Ajlan. And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn Hakim except Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad."
"2217","2208 - Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Anbasa al-Warraq narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Thabit, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father: that Qayla bint al-Uzza sent to her daughter Asma bint Abi Bakr - and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, had divorced her in Jahiliyya - sending gifts including cottage cheese and ghee; but she refused to accept her gift or let her into her house. So she sent to A'isha to ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Let her into her house and accept her gift."" And Allah, blessed and exalted, revealed, ""Allah does not forbid you concerning those who did not fight you in religion"" - the verse. And we do not know for this hadith any route from Ibn al-Zubayr except this route."
"2218","2209 - Some of our companions narrated to us, from Bishr ibn al-Sari, he said: Mus'ab ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: ""This verse was revealed: 'And no one has with Him any favor to be recompensed, except seeking the Face of his Lord, the Most High, and he shall surely be pleased' concerning Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him."" And we do not know for this hadith any route from Ibn al-Zubayr except this route, and we do not know anyone narrated it except Bishr, from Mus'ab ibn Thabit."
"2219","2210 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us: Hunayd ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave me the blood, saying: ""Go and hide it."" So I went and drank it, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said to me: ""What did you do with it?"" I said: I hid it. He said: ""Perhaps you drank it?"" I said: I drank it. And this account has been narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr through another route."
"2220","2211 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to point with his little finger when he gave the sermon. And we do not know this hadith narrated except from Ibn al-Zubayr, and we do not know for it any route from Ibn al-Zubayr except this route."
"2221","2212 - Yahya ibn Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father: that Quraysh said: ""The likeness of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is like a palm tree in a dunghill (kabwa)."""
"2222","2213 - Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Karkhi narrated to us: Hamid ibn Yahya al-Balkhi narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sa'd, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: ""This is Allah's freed one (atiq) from the Fire."" So on that day he was named Atiq, and his name before that was Abd Allah ibn Uthman. And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith with this chain except Hamid, from Ibn Uyayna."
"2223","2214 - Abd Allah ibn Abi Raja narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Aswad, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Announce marriage and beat upon it the ghirbal"" - meaning the duff. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr except through this route with this chain."
"2224","Abd Allah ibn Urwa from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr 2215 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir, from al-Zuhri, from Abd Allah ibn Urwa, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It was only named al-Bayt al-Atiq (the Ancient Freed House) because it was freed from tyrants; no tyrant ever attained it, or no tyrant was able over it."" And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from Ibn al-Zubayr from him, and we do not know for it any route from Ibn al-Zubayr except this route."
"2225","Mus'ab ibn Thabit from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr 2216 - al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Sukayn narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us: Musa ibn Ubayda narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Thabit, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people laughing and said: ""Do you laugh while the mention of Paradise and Hell is among you?"" He said: so none of them was seen laughing until he died. He said: and concerning them was revealed, ""Inform My servants that I am the Forgiving, the Merciful, and that My punishment is the painful punishment."" And we do not know anyone narrates it with this wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ibn al-Zubayr, and we do not know for it any route except this route; and we do not know that Mus'ab ibn Thabit heard from Ibn al-Zubayr."
"2226","2217 - Muhammad ibn Mirdas al-Ansari narrated to us: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Thabit, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he broke fast with people, would say: ""The fasting ones have broken fast with you, the righteous have eaten your food, and the angels have prayed upon you."" And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr except from the narration of Mus'ab ibn Thabit from him, and we heard this hadith only from Muhammad ibn Mirdas, from Abd al-Wahhab."
"2227","2218 - And others besides Muhammad narrate it from Abd al-Wahhab, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Mus'ab ibn Thabit, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as Ibn Mirdas narrated it from Abd al-Wahhab. Muhammad ibn Ali al-Ahwazi narrated it to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Yahya narrated to us."
"2228","Nafi' ibn Thabit from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr 2219 - Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us: Mansur ibn Salama al-Khuza'i narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawal narrated to us: Nafi' ibn Thabit narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed Isha, would pray four rak'as and make witr with one prostration (sajda), then sleep until he prayed afterwards his night prayer."" And we do not know anyone narrates this hadith with this wording except Ibn al-Zubayr, and we do not know for it any route from Ibn al-Zubayr better than this route."
"2229","Hanzala ibn Qays from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr 2220 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us: Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah al-Zubayri narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Mus'ab ibn Thabit, from Hanzala ibn Qays, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."" And we do not know this statement narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this route with this chain."
"2230","Thabit al-Bunani from Ibn al-Zubayr 2221 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: ""Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade silk."" And similar to this statement has been narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. And we do not know Thabit narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr anything except this hadith."
"2231","Al-Abbas ibn Sahl from Ibn al-Zubayr 2222 - Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn informed us: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil narrated to us: al-Abbas ibn Sahl narrated to me, he said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr saying: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth he would wish for a second valley with it; and if he had a second he would wish for a third with it; and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust."" And we do not know this statement narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr except through this route with this chain."
"2232","Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhita from Ibn al-Zubayr 2223 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhita, he said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr saying: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded fasting the day of Ashura."""
"2233","2224 - And Ma'mar ibn Sahl narrated it to us: Mus'ab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhita, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. And we do not know this statement narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr except through this route; and Thuwayr - Shu'ba and Isra'il and others narrated from him and accepted his hadith."
"2234","Subay' - unnamed - from Ibn al-Zubayr 2225 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us: Mukhawwal ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Subay', from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2235","2226 - And Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated it to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Subay', from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Before the Hour there will be thirty lying impostors (dajjals)."" And we do not know anyone who made this hadith precise (jawwadahu) except Qays; and more than one narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from one who heard Ibn al-Zubayr."
"2236","Abd al-Aziz ibn Usayd from Ibn al-Zubayr 2227 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Maslama, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Usayd, from Ibn al-Zubayr: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the jar (al-jarr). And this Abd al-Aziz ibn Usayd - we do not know anyone narrated from him except Abu Maslama; and the prohibition of nabidh of the jar has been narrated through another route."
"2237","Abu al-Hakam al-Bajali from him 2228 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Hakam, he said: I asked Ibn al-Zubayr, and he said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the jar and the gourd (al-dubba)."" He said: and I asked Ibn Umar, and he said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the jar, the gourd, and the pitch-coated vessel (al-muzaffat)."" He said: and my brother narrated to me from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the jar, the gourd, and the pitch-coated vessel, and (mixing) unripe dates and ripe dates. And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith from Abu al-Hakam except Salama ibn Kuhayl."
"2238","Abu al-Ward from Ibn al-Zubayr 2229 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us: Sa'id ibn al-Hakam narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'a informed us: al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to me that Abu al-Ward narrated to him that he heard Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr saying: that the tashahhud of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with which he would make tashahhud was: ""In the name of Allah, and by Allah, the best of names; greetings, good words, and prayers belong to Allah. I bear witness there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger; He sent him with the truth as a bringer of glad tidings and a warner; and the Hour is coming, no doubt in it. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. O Allah, forgive me and guide me."" And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording concerning the tashahhud of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from Ibn al-Zubayr with this chain; and as for Abu al-Ward, we do not know anyone narrated from him except al-Harith ibn Yazid; and al-Harith ibn Yazid - Ibn Lahi'a and others narrated from him."
"2239","Abu al-Zubayr from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr 2230 - Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, the freedman of Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Ibn al-Zubayr."
"2240","2231 - And Isma'il ibn Hafs narrated it to us: Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ibn al-Zubayr: that he used to say at the end of his prayer when he gave salam: ""There is no god but Allah alone without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable; there is no change nor power except through Allah; we worship none but Him; to Him belong blessing, favor, and fine praise, sincere to Him in religion though the disbelievers dislike it."" He said: ""And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to proclaim Allah's greatness with them at the end of every prayer."" And we do not know this hadith narrated except from Ibn al-Zubayr with this wording."
"2241","Ya'ish ibn al-Walid, freedman of Ibn al-Zubayr, from him 2232 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Musa ibn Khalaf narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ya'ish ibn al-Walid, freedman of Ibn al-Zubayr, from Ibn al-Zubayr: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There has crept to you the disease of the nations before you: hatred and envy; and hatred is the shaver - not the shaver of hair, but the shaver of religion. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not inform you - I think, of what will establish you - spread salam among you."" And Musa ibn Khalaf differed in its chain from Hisham, the author of al-Dustuwa'i: Hisham narrated it from Yahya, from Ya'ish ibn al-Walid, from the freedman of al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr; while Musa said: from Yahya, from Ya'ish, freedman of Ibn al-Zubayr, from Ibn al-Zubayr. And Hisham is more retentive (ahfaz)."
"2242","A man from Ibn al-Zubayr 2233 - Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Sinan ibn Habib, from a man, from Ibn al-Zubayr: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command the siwak. And we do not know this statement narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr except through this route."
"2243","Musnad Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far 2234 - Musa ibn Abd Allah Abu Talha al-Khuza'i narrated to us: Bakr ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Hakim, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""It is not fitting for a servant to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta."""
"2244","2235 - And Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq. 2236 - And Sa'id ibn Nuh narrated it to us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, from Isma'il ibn Abi Hakim, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far except with this chain."
"2245","2237 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us: Hanzala narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, he said: ""He forbade killing house snakes (al-jinnan) - I think he said - those in houses."""
"2246","2238 - And al-Qasim narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, similarly. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far except with this chain."
"2247","2239 - And Azhar ibn Jamil narrated it to us: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Hanzala, from al-Qasim, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, he said: ""They were forbidden to be killed,"" meaning the house snakes in houses."
"2248","Urwa ibn al-Zubayr from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far 2240 - Ibrahim ibn Malik al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, he said: ""I saw the Prophet eating cucumber with fresh dates."" And this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwa - we do not know anyone narrated it from him except Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar, a man from Kufa, no harm in him; and we heard it only from Ibrahim ibn Malik from him."
"2249","Al-Sha'bi from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far 2241 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Usama narrated to us: Junayd ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I asked Abd Allah ibn Ja'far about the bequest - meaning did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) make a bequest? He said: ""I never heard of it until I came to this land of yours."" And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith except Abu Usama from Junayd."
"2250","Muwarriq al-Ijli from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far 2242 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Muwarriq al-Ijli, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, he said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seated me behind him, and the son(s) of Fatimah - or one of the two sons of Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her - on a mount."" And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far with a better chain than this."
"2251","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far 2243 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan, known as Ibn Abi Ali al-Kirmani, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Sufyan al-Aslami narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The hand of Allah is with the debtor until he pays his debt, so long as it is not in something Allah dislikes."" And we do not know this statement narrated with this wording except by Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this chain."
"2252","2244 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shayban, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped on the crown of his head while in ihram. And we do not know this wording narrated except from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far with this chain."
"2253","Khalid ibn Sara from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far 2245 - Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyayna informed us: Ja'far ibn Khalid ibn Sara narrated to us, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Make food for the family of Ja'far, for there has come to them what occupies them"" - or a matter that occupies them - meaning the day the news of Ja'far's death came, may Allah be pleased with him."
"2254","2246 - And Ahmad ibn Abda narrated it to us: Sufyan informed us, from Ja'far ibn Khalid, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried two boys from Banu Abd al-Muttalib on a mount. And this Ja'far ibn Khalid - Ibn Jurayj and Ibn Uyayna narrated from him."
"2255","Sa'd ibn Ibrahim from him 2247 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, he said: ""I saw the Prophet eating cucumber with fresh dates."" And we do not know Sa'd ibn Ibrahim narrated from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far anything except this hadith."
"2256","Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Ja'far from his father 2248 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Abu Amir narrated to us: Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from his father, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Prompt your dying ones with: there is no god but Allah."" And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far except through this route."
"2257","Isma'il ibn Abd Allah ibn Ja'far from his father 2249 - Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: Ibn Abi Mulayka, meaning Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Mulayka, narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from his father, he said: when Ja'far came from Abyssinia the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him and kissed between his eyes, saying: ""I am not more joyful at the conquest of Khaybar than I am at the arrival of Ja'far,"" may Allah be pleased with him. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this route; and al-Sha'bi narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from his father."
"2258","2250 - Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Shayba narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated to us: Ibn Abi Mulayka narrated to me, from Isma'il ibn Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from his father, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O people, repent to Allah, blessed and exalted, for I repent every day seventy times."" And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far except with this chain."
"2259","2251 - Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Shayba narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: Ibn Abi Mulayka narrated to me, from Isma'il ibn Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from his father, he said: when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw mercy descending he said: ""Who will supplicate for me?"" His daughter said: I will, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""Call Ali,"" may Allah be pleased with him. So Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them, were called; he placed al-Hasan on his right, al-Husayn on his left, and Fatimah facing him, then covered them with a cloak, then said: ""These are my household (ahl)."" So Allah, blessed and exalted, revealed, ""Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and purify you thoroughly."" And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far except through this route."
"2260","2252 - Najih ibn Ibrahim al-Kufi narrated to us: Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Mulayka narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: ""Allah, blessed and exalted, commanded me to bring you near and not distance you, to teach you and not be harsh with you."" And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far except with this chain."
"2261","2253 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us: Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah al-Zubayri narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Isma'il ibn Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from his father, he said: ""I saw upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two yellow garments."" And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far except with this chain."
"2262","Mu'awiya ibn Abd Allah ibn Ja'far from his father 2254 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Mu'awiya ibn Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from his father, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not take living things containing a soul as targets."" And this statement has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through more than one route. And we do not know it narrated from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far except through this route with this chain."
"2263","2255 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Mu'awiya ibn Abd Allah ibn Ja'far - I think - from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Uhud while burying Hamza ibn Abd al-Muttalib, may Allah be pleased with him - a striped cloak (namira) was brought to shroud him in, and his feet showed, so he covered his head and placed upon his feet - I think he said - idhkhir (a fragrant grass) - then buried him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Were it not that our women would grieve at that, I would have left you in the open for the birds and beasts generally."" And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far except through this route with this chain."
"2264","Ibn Aqil from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far 2256 - al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Yahya ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Ibn Aqil - meaning Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil - from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear his ring on his right hand. And we do not know anyone narrated it from Ibn Aqil except Yahya ibn al-Ala."
"2265","Al-Hasan ibn Sa'd from him 2257 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Ya'qub, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the army of commanders, saying: ""Then Ja'far took the banner and was struck down; then Zayd ibn Haritha took it and was struck down; then Abd Allah ibn Rawaha took it and was struck down; then a sword from the swords of Allah, blessed and exalted - Khalid ibn al-Walid - took it."" And we do not know anyone narrated this account from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abd Allah ibn Ja'far."
"2266","2258 - Fitr ibn Hammad ibn Waqid narrated to us: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Ya'qub, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, he said: ""When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to relieve himself he liked to shield himself with a wall or a dense grove of palms; so he seated me behind him, then went to the base of a wall and shielded himself."" And similar to this account has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through more than one route; and we do not know it narrated from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far except through this route with this chain."
"2267","Ibn Abi Rafi' from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far 2259 - Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us: Ibn Abi Rafi' narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing his ring on his right hand. And this Ibn Abi Rafi' - Hammad ibn Salama narrated from him more than one hadith. And this hadith was narrated from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far by Ibn Abi Rafi' and Ibn Aqil."
"2268","Budayh, freedman of Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far 2260 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Umar ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us: Juwayriya ibn Asma narrated to us, from Isa ibn Umar, from Budayh, freedman of Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he named al-Madina ""Taba."" And this hadith contains other speech, so we abridged from it the raised (marfu') portion; and we do not know it narrated from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far except with this chain."
"2269","A shaykh from Fahm called Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far 2261 - Amr narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Mis'ar, he said: a shaykh from Fahm narrated to me - Yahya said: his name is Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman - from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best meat is the meat of the back."" And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Mis'ar, from a shaykh from Fahm; and we do not know anyone who named him except Yahya ibn Sa'id."
"2270","2262 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from Raqaba ibn Masqala, from a shaykh from Fahm, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best meat is the meat of the back."" And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith from Raqaba except Jarir."
"2271","Musnad Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them both; Musnad Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him; Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr 2263 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib narrated to us: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr: that the People of the Suffa were poor people, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever has food for two, let him go with three; and whoever has food for four, let him go with five"" - or as he said. And Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, came with three, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went with ten; and Abu Bakr with three. He said: they were me, my father, my mother - he said: and I do not know whether he said - and the servant of our house and the house of Abu Bakr. And Abu Bakr dined with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then remained until he prayed Isha with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then returned and came after as much of the night as Allah willed had passed. His wife said: what kept you from your guests? - or she said: your guest? He said: did you not give them supper? She said: they refused until you came; it had been offered to them. He said: so I went and hid. He said: O ghunthar (dullard)! He said: so he became distressed and swore, saying: eat; by Allah I will never taste it. They said: by Allah, we would not eat until you ate. He said: so he took; by Allah, we would not take a morsel except it grew from beneath it. He said: so we ate to fullness and it became more than it was before that. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, looked at it and it was as it was or more. He said to his mother: O sister of Banu Firas, what is this? She said: no, by the delight of my eye, it is more than it was before that by three times. And Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, ate from it, saying: that was from Satan - meaning his oath - then he ate a morsel from it, then carried it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it remained with him in the morning. He said: and there was between us and some people a pact; the term expired, so we dispatched twelve men, with each man of them - Allah knows how many followed each man of them - except that he is counted; so they all ate. And we do not know anyone narrates this hadith except Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr. And this chain is among the best chains narrated in that from Abd al-Rahman."
"2272","2264 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Abu Uthman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, he said: we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one hundred and thirty men. He said: ""Does any of you have food?"" He said: so dough was kneaded, then a tall polytheist man came with sheep. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Is it sale or gift?"" - or he said: present? He said: no, rather sale. He said: ""So he bought a sheep from him."" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the liver (sawad al-batn) and it was lightly cooked (umlikha); by Allah, there was not one of the one hundred and thirty except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut for him a cut of its liver; if he was present he gave him, and if he was absent he kept for him. He said: and he made from it two bowls; so we all ate and were satisfied, and there remained in the bowl, and he carried it upon the camel. And we do not know this account narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr."
"2273","2265 - And Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated it to us: Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Razin informed us: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith from Shu'ba except Amr ibn Muhammad."
"2274","Amr ibn Aws from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr 2266 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Amr ibn Aws, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to make A'isha perform umra from al-Tan'im. And we do not know Amr ibn Aws narrated from Abd al-Rahman any supported hadith except this hadith."
"2275","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr 2267 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Bakr narrated to us: Mubarak ibn Fadala narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: ""Who among you woke up today fasting?"" Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I intended last night and woke up fasting. He said: ""Who gave charity today?"" Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I did; a beggar knocked and I entered and there was a morsel in Abd al-Rahman's hand, so I took it and gave it to him. He said: ""Which of you today visited a sick person?"" Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I did; it was said to me that Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn Awf - was sick, so I went and visited him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""These qualities never combine in a man in one day except he enters Paradise."" And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr except with this chain; others besides Abd Allah ibn Bakr narrate it from Mubarak, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla as mursal; and we heard it connected (muttasil) only from Bishr ibn Adam, from Abd Allah ibn Bakr."
"2276","Maymun ibn Mihran from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr 2268 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Mihran, from Musa ibn Ubayd, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""My Lord, blessed and exalted, gave me seventy thousand of my umma who enter Paradise without reckoning."" Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: why did you not ask Him for more? He said: ""I did ask Him for more, and He gave me with each"" - meaning thousand - ""seventy thousand."" He said: why did you not ask Him for more? He said: ""I did ask Him for more, and He gave me with each man seventy thousand."" Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: why did you not ask Him for more? He said: ""He gave me thus,"" and he spread his arm span, saying: ""This is from Allah, blessed and exalted; its number is not known."" And we do not know this statement narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr except through this route with this chain."
"2277","Hafsa bint Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr from her father 2269 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us: Ibn Abi Maryam and Dawud ibn Mihran narrated to us - the wording is Ibn Abi Maryam's - they said: Dawud, that is Ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar, informed us: Abd Allah ibn Uthman, meaning Ibn Khuthaym, narrated to me, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hafsa bint Abd al-Rahman, from her father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abd al-Rahman: ""Seat your sister behind you and make her perform umra from al-Tan'im; when she descends from the hillock, order her to enter ihram, for it is an accepted umra."""
"2278","2270 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us: Abu Ishaq al-Talqani narrated to us - Abu Bakr said, whose name is Ibrahim ibn Isa - he said: Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hafsa bint Abd al-Rahman, from her father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned similarly. And we do not know Hafsa narrated from her father anything except this hadith."
"2279","Abu Thawr from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr 2271 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us: Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us - I think - from Bukayr, from Bakr ibn Sawada, from Abu Thawr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, he said: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Charity is not lawful for a rich person, nor for one of sound strength - or strong."" And this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr has been narrated through this route and through another route."
"2280","The judge of the two cities from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr - and I think he is Shurayh ... ibn Qays 2272 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh and Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, they said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Sadaqa ibn Musa informed us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Qays ibn Zayd, he said: the judge of the two cities narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, blessed and exalted, will call the debtor on the Day of Resurrection and station him before Him, saying, blessed and exalted: O servant, in what did you squander people's wealth? He will say: O Lord, You know I did not spoil it; it only went in drowning, burning, or theft. So Allah, blessed and exalted, will call for something and place it in his scale, and his good deeds will outweigh."" And we do not know this statement narrated except from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this chain."
"2281","Abd Allah al-Bahiyy, freedman of Ibn al-Zubayr, from Abd al-Rahman 2273 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Abd Allah al-Bahiyy, freedman of al-Zubayr, he said: I was in the mosque while Marwan was giving the sermon, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr said: by Allah, he did not appoint as successor anyone of his household. Marwan said: you are the one about whom was revealed, ""And the one who says to his parents: Fie upon you."" Abd al-Rahman said: ""You lied; rather the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed your father."" And we do not know this statement narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this route. End of the Musnad of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, which is the end of the twenty-first - and praise be to Allah abundantly."
"2282","Musnad Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, may Allah be pleased with him 2274 - Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq al-Bazzar narrated to me, he said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us: my father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan narrating from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2283","2275 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn al-Uryan, narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from al-Hasan, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura said: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2284","2276 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2285","2277 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us: Jarir, meaning Ibn Abd al-Hamid, narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2286","2278 - And Ali ibn Muslim al-Tusi narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Yunus ibn Ubayd and Mansur ibn Zadham informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2287","2279 - And Tamim ibn al-Muntasir al-Wasiti narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, meaning Ibn Harb, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2288","2280 - And Abu Kamil narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan and Simak ibn Atiyya, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2289","2281 - And al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us: al-Minhal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd and Habib, meaning Ibn al-Shahid, and Thabit al-Bunani, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2290","2282 - And Ibrahim ibn Bistam al-Za'farani narrated it to us: Abu Asim narrated to us: Sahl al-Sarraj narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2291","2283 - And Yahya ibn Khalaf Abu Salama narrated to us: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2292","2284 - And Ja'far ibn Muhammad, nephew of Waki' ibn al-Jarrah, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bashir narrated to us: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2293","2285 - And Abu Bujayr Muhammad ibn Jabir ibn Bujayr narrated to us: Abu Usama narrated to us: Awf and Isma'il ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2294","2286 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Bakr ibn Bakkar narrated to us: Abu Hurra narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2295","2287 - And Muhammad ibn al-Mu'ammal al-Haddadi narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Qurra narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2296","2288 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2297","2289 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us: Mubarak ibn Fadala narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2298","2290 - And Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Ziyad al-Jassas, that is Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad, informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2299","2291 - And Ma'mar ibn Sahl narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Kufi narrated to us: Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2300","2292 - And Ali ibn Qurra ibn Habib narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from al-Sari ibn Yahya, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and their wordings are close - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""O Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for leadership; if you are given it upon asking, you will be left to it, and if you are given it without asking, you will be helped in it. And when you swear an oath and see another better than it, do what is better and expiate for your oath."" Abu Bakr said: others besides those we named narrated it from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura. As for the hadith of al-Taymi from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, we do not know anyone narrated it except al-Mu'tamir from his father. As for the hadith of Ibn Awn, al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Rahman connected it; and Ibn Abi Adi narrated it from Ibn Awn, from al-Hasan: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abd al-Rahman. As for the hadith of Hisham, a group narrated it from Hisham, from al-Hasan. As for the hadith of Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir from al-Hasan, Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir did not support (musnad) from al-Hasan any hadith besides this one. As for the hadith of Mansur ibn Zadham, none narrated it from him except Hushaym. As for the hadith of Yunus from al-Hasan, more than one narrated it from Yunus, so we sufficed with Hushaym. As for the hadith of Humayd, Thabit and Habib from al-Hasan, none narrated it except Hammad ibn Salama. As for the hadith of Simak from al-Hasan, none narrated it except Sharik from Simak. As for the hadith of Simak ibn Atiyya, we do not know anyone narrated it except Hammad ibn Zayd; and Simak ibn Atiyya did not support from al-Hasan any hadith except this one. As for the hadith of Sahl al-Sarraj from al-Hasan, Sahl al-Sarraj did not support from al-Hasan any hadith besides this one, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Sahl except Abu Asim. As for the hadith of Ali ibn Zayd from al-Hasan, Mis'ar and Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiya narrated it from Ali ibn Zayd; we mentioned it from Mis'ar and sufficed, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Mis'ar, from Ali ibn Zayd, except Muhammad ibn Bishr and Abu Dawud al-Hafari. As for the hadith of Qatada from al-Hasan, it is only retained from the hadith of Sa'id, from Qatada. As for the hadith of Qurra from al-Hasan, we do not know anyone narrated it except Muslim from Qurra. As for the hadith of Awf and Isma'il ibn Muslim, that is only retained from the hadith of Abu Usama. As for the hadith of al-Sari ibn Yahya, we retain it only from the hadith of Qurra ibn Habib. As for the hadith of Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari, we retain it only from the hadith of Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Kufi from Yazid ibn Ibrahim. As for the hadith of Ziyad al-Jassas from al-Hasan, we retain it only from the hadith of Yazid ibn Harun from Ziyad. As for the hadith of Jarir ibn Hazim, we retain it only from the hadith of Wahb from his father; and the hadith of Mubarak from al-Hasan was narrated by more than one from al-Mubarak."
"2301","Musnad Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, may Allah be pleased with him; Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir 2293 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Shaddad ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, from his father, he said: ""I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying standing and sitting."""
"2302","2294 - And Abu Burayd Amr ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam ibn Tahman narrated to us: Sayyar Abu al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: I heard Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir narrating from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate saying, ""O Allah, grant me enjoyment of my hearing and sight, and make them the inheritor from me."" And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir except with this chain."
"2303","2295 - And Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us: al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father, he said: ""I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in his sandals, then spit, then rubbed it with his sandal."" And this hadith - thus Yazid narrated it from al-Jurayri; and a group narrated it from al-Jurayri, from Yazid, from Mutarrif, from his father."
"2304","Musnad Abu Usayd, may Allah be pleased with him; from the hadith of Abu Usayd 2296 - Amr ibn Malik narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'a, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'a, from Irak ibn Malik. 2297 - And Amr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Mundhir ibn Abi Usayd, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Mecca, Abu Mahdhura came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to call the adhan. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Call."" Bilal used to call; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned, Abu Mahdhura stayed behind. And we do not know anyone narrates this hadith with this wording except Abu Usayd, and we do not know anyone connected it except al-Waqidi; and people narrated from al-Waqidi though they criticized him, and they did not establish proof against him except by supposition; and in his hadith there is oddness (nakara)."
"2305","2298 - Amr narrated to us: al-Waqidi narrated to us: Ubayy ibn Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, he said: I heard Abu Usayd saying: ""I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twenty raids, one raid after another."" And we do not know this account narrated except from Abu Usayd, and we do not know for Abu Usayd any route besides this route; and our mention of al-Waqidi has preceded."
"2306","2299 - Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman: that he heard Abu Usayd: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar."""
"2307","Musnad Abu al-Yasar, may Allah be pleased with him; in the name of Allah, the Merciful, the Compassionate; may Allah bless Muhammad, His noble Messenger, and his family and grant abundant peace. From the hadith of Abu al-Yasar 2300 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Jabala informed us: Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Sharik, from Uthman ibn Mawhab, from Musa ibn Talha, from Abu al-Yasar, he said: I met a woman and embraced her, though I did not have intercourse with her. I came to Umar and asked him; he said: fear Allah, conceal yourself, and inform no one. He said: I could not bear it until I came to Abu Bakr and asked him; he said: fear Allah, conceal yourself, and inform no one. I could not bear it until I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: ""Did you equip a warrior?"" I said: no. He said: ""Did you take the place of a warrior among his family?"" I said: no. He kept speaking to me until I wished I had entered Islam at that hour. When I turned away he called me and recited to me, ""And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the watches of the night."" His companions said: is this for him specifically or for people generally? He said: ""Rather for people generally."" And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except from Abu al-Yasar; and we do not know anyone narrated it from Abu al-Yasar except Musa ibn Talha, nor from Musa except Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Mawhab; and Sharik and Qays narrated it from Uthman. We mentioned the hadith of Sharik because he was greater than Qays, and sufficed with it. And we do not know this speech narrated except from him; and something similar has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with differing wording, which we shall mention in its place, Allah willing."
"2308","2301 - Amr narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Wahb informed us, from Ibn Lahi'a, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'a, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu al-Yasar, may Allah be pleased with him: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade steeping dates and raisins together."" And this hadith - Ibn Lahi'a said in it: from Ja'far, from Irak, from Abu al-Yasar; while others besides Ibn Lahi'a said: from Irak, from Abu Hurayra. So we mentioned the hadith of Abu al-Yasar since it is the rarer hadith; and perhaps the hadith of Abu Hurayra contains an addition which we shall mention in its place with its addition, Allah willing."
"2309","2302 - Amr narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Sulayman informed us: Yazid ibn Amir ibn Abi al-Yasar informed us, from his father, from Abu al-Yasar, may Allah be pleased with him: that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed that admits me to Paradise. He said: ""Withhold this"" - pointing to his tongue. He repeated it to him, and he said: ""May your mother be bereaved of you! Does anything topple people upon their nostrils into the Fire except the harvests of their tongues?"" Abu Bakr said: and we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu al-Yasar except through this route; and we do not know anyone narrated it except Amr ibn Malik, from Fudayl ibn Sulayman. We heard no one follow him in this hadith, nor did we see it with anyone else with a chain different from this chain, so we would know he erred in it - or he may be correct. Since we knew no defect in it, we mentioned it, as its chain is fair (hasan) and its text is strange (gharib)."
"2310","2303 - Amr ibn Malik narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Wahb informed us: Amr ibn al-Harith informed us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Umar ibn al-Hakam, from Abu al-Yasar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man prays a prayer and gets of it half of it, a third, a fourth, a fifth, a sixth, a seventh, an eighth, a ninth, a tenth."" Abu Bakr said: and we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith saying ""from Abu al-Yasar"" except Ibn Wahb, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Umar ibn al-Hakam. And more than one narrated it saying: from Umar ibn al-Hakam, from Ammar ibn Yasir. So we mentioned this hadith from Abu al-Yasar; and in the hadith of Ammar there was an addition; and the hadith of Abu al-Yasar is little, so we mentioned it to make known that Abu al-Yasar narrated it, and we clarified the defect in it."
"2311","2304 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us: Harun ibn Ma'ruf informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us: Makhrama ibn Bukayr narrated to me, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Nafi', he said: Abu al-Yasar saw me praying Duha prayer when the sun had risen, and forbade me, then said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not pray until the sun rises high, for it rises between the two horns of Satan."" Abu Bakr said: and we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu al-Yasar except through this route; and something similar has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with other than this wording. So we mentioned the hadith of Abu al-Yasar for this defect; and as for Sa'id ibn Nafi', we do not know anyone narrated from him except Bukayr ibn Abd Allah."
"2312","Musnad Sahl ibn Abi Hathma, may Allah be pleased with him; Sahl ibn Abi Hathma 2305 - Amr informed us: Abu Dawud informed us: Shu'ba informed us: Khubayb, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, informed me: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Mas'ud ibn Niyar, he said: Sahl ibn Abi Hathma came to us and said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you estimate (the crop), take, and leave a third; if you do not leave a third, leave a fourth."" Abu Bakr said: and we do not know anyone narrated this hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Sahl ibn Abi Hathma; and we do not know anyone narrates this hadith from Sahl except Abd al-Rahman ibn Niyar - and he is known; and we do not know anyone narrated it except Shu'ba."
"2313","Musnad Amr ibn al-Hamiq, may Allah be pleased with him; from the hadith of Amr ibn al-Hamiq 2306 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Abu Awana informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rifa'a ibn Shaddad, he said: I heard Amr ibn al-Hamiq al-Khuza'i saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whoever grants a man security for his life then kills him, he will carry a banner of treachery on the Day of Resurrection."" And this hadith was narrated by Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Rifa'a ibn Shaddad, who is Rifa'a al-Qitbani from whom al-Suddi narrated. As for the hadith of Qurra, Qurra erred in it because he said: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Amir ibn Shaddad; the correct is what Abu Awana said; and others besides Abu Awana followed him in similar to his narration, so we sufficed with Abu Awana alone."
"2314","2307 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir and Abu Amir informed us, from Qurra, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Amir ibn Shaddad, from Amr ibn al-Hamiq, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"2315","2308 - Bishr ibn Khalid and Ahmad ibn Uthman narrated to us, they said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us: Isa ibn Umar informed us, from al-Suddi, from Rifa'a al-Qitbani, from Amr ibn al-Hamiq, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whoever grants a man security for his life then kills him, I am innocent of the killer, even if the slain was a disbeliever."" Abu Bakr said: and we only mentioned this hadith from Amr ibn al-Hamiq because it differs in wording from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr said, ""Whoever grants a man security for his life then kills him, he will carry a banner of treachery""; while Isa said, ""I am innocent of the killer,"" so it became another hadith. Abu Bakr said: and Sulayman al-Taymi narrated from al-Suddi, from Rifa'a, from Amr ibn al-Hamiq, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly to the hadith of Isa ibn Umar from Rifa'a, from Amr."
"2316","2309 - So Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us with the hadith of Sulayman al-Taymi: Amr ibn Asim informed us: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, from his father, from al-Suddi, from Rifa'a, from Amr ibn al-Hamiq, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2317","2310 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us: Mu'awiya ibn Salih informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Amr ibn al-Hamiq, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When Allah intends good for a servant, He sweetens him with honey (assalahu)."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is His sweetening him? He said: ""He guides him to a righteous deed, then takes him upon it."""
"2318","2311 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Salih informed us: Abu Shurayh Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh informed us that he heard Umayra ibn Abd Allah al-Ma'afiri saying: my father narrated to me that he heard Ibn al-Hamiq saying: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will be a tribulation in which the safest of people - or he said: the best of people - are the western army (al-jund al-gharbi)."" Ibn al-Hamiq said: that is why I came to you in Egypt. And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith with this wording except Amr ibn al-Hamiq alone. And we do not know for it any route except this route; and we do not know anyone narrated it from Ibn Shurayh except Abd Allah ibn Salih."
"2319","Musnad Abd Allah ibn Buhayna, may Allah be pleased with him 2312 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ruwayn informed us: Attaf ibn Khalid informed us: Malik ibn Abd Allah ibn Buhayna narrated to me, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought forgiveness and prayed upon the people of a graveyard in Asqalan. And Muhammad ibn Ruwayn is Basran; we do not know him to narrate much; and Attaf is weak."
"2320","2313 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us: the nephew of Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from his uncle, from al-A'raj, from Ibn Buhayna, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer in which he recited aloud; when he finished he said: ""Do you recite behind me?"" Some of them said: indeed we do. He said: ""Do not do so; I say: what is wrong with me that I am being contended with for the Qur'an?"" He said: so the people refrained from reciting in what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited aloud in. And we do not know anyone who said in it ""from al-Zuhri, from al-A'raj"" except the nephew of al-Zuhri, and he erred in it; it is rather from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ukayma. Thus Ibn Uyayna and Ma'mar narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ukayma, from Abu Hurayra. But we mentioned the hadith of Ibn Buhayna so that whoever hears that knows it is an error."
"2321","Musnad of Ruwayfi ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him). Ruwayfi ibn Thabit 2314 - Yahya ibn Khalaf Abu Salama narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Hasan, from Ruwayfi ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not irrigate what another sows."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Ruwayfi ibn Thabit alone, so its chain is hasan."
"2322","2315 - Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud, and Amr ibn Khalid, and Yahya ibn Bukayr informed us, they said: Ibn Lahia informed us, he said: Bakr ibn Sawada narrated to me, from Ziyad ibn Nuaym, from Wafa ibn Shurayh al-Hadrami, from Ruwayfi ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever sends blessings upon Muhammad and says: O Allah, grant him the near station with You on the Day of Resurrection, my intercession becomes due for him."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except Ruwayfi ibn Thabit alone."
"2323","2316 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Asad ibn Musa informed us, he said: Idris ibn Yahya al-Khawlani informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ayyash informed us, from his father, from Shiyaym ibn Baytan, from Shayban ibn Umayya, from Ruwayfi ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whomever an evil omen turns back from something has committed shirk."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it with this wording except Ruwayfi ibn Thabit alone, and Shiyaym ibn Baytan is not well known, and we only mentioned his hadith since these words are not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from him, and he has narrated other hadiths besides this one as well."
"2324","2317 - Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Fadala informed us, he said: Ayyash ibn Abbas informed us, from Shiyaym ibn Baytan, from Shayban, he said: We were with Ruwayfi ibn Thabit, and he said: ""I shall surely come to know that someone has tied a watar (a knotted string) or cleaned himself with a bone or dung; whoever does that has disassociated himself from Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or from what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" And this hadith, similar words have been narrated by more than one, but as for this wording, it is not preserved from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor from anyone other than Ruwayfi, and it was included in the Musnad because he said: he has disassociated from what was revealed to Muhammad, and its chain is hasan, except for Shayban, for we do not know anyone who narrated from him except Shiyaym ibn Baytan, and Ayyash ibn Abbas is well known."
"2325","Musnad of Uthman ibn Abi al-As (may Allah be pleased with him). From the hadith of Uthman ibn Abi al-As 2318 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us, he said: Shuba informed us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: ""The last thing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me, when I lead a people in prayer, was to lighten the prayer for them."" And this hadith has been narrated from Uthman ibn Abi al-As through several ways, and the highest of them in chain that is narrated in this regard is this chain, and we do not know that Said ibn al-Musayyib narrated from Uthman ibn Abi al-As any hadith other than this one, nor did anyone narrate it from Said ibn al-Musayyib except Amr ibn Murra, nor from Amr except Shuba, so we mentioned this chain from Uthman to the exclusion of the other chains narrated from him in this regard, except that where Yazid adds something, it is written on account of the addition."
"2326","2319 - Yahya ibn Khalaf Abu Salama narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Said ibn Abi Hind, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Fasting is a shield, like the shield of one of you in fighting - or from fighting."" He said: And the last thing the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me when he sent me to Taif was that he said: ""O Uthman, when you lead a people, be brief with them in prayer, and measure them by the weakest among them."" And this hadith, we only wrote it because its wording differs from the wording of Said ibn al-Musayyib from Uthman, and for that reason we mentioned it, and had it been the same, the hadith of Said from Uthman would have sufficed. And in this hadith there is also ""Fasting is a shield,"" which is not in the hadith of Said ibn al-Musayyib from Uthman, so we mentioned it on account of the addition in it and the difference in its wording."
"2327","2320 - Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, in the night there is an hour in which a caller calls out: Is there any supplicant so I may answer him? Is there any asker so I may give him? Is there any seeker of forgiveness so I may forgive him?"" And this hadith, similar words have been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with different wordings; we shall mention each hadith among them with its wording in its place, Allah willing, and we do not know anyone who narrates this hadith from Uthman ibn Abi al-As except through this way with this chain."
"2328","2321 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid informed us, he said: Anbasa ibn Abi Raita informed us, from al-Hasan, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Fasting is a shield with which the servant shields himself from the Fire."" And this hadith, we have mentioned similar words from Uthman, but the first hadith of Uthman is ""Fasting is a shield like the shield of one of you from fighting,"" while in this hadith it is: ""with which the servant shields himself from the Fire,"" so we mentioned that due to the difference of wording in it."
"2329","2322 - Muhammad ibn Mirdas and Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, they said: Salim ibn Nuh informed us, he said: al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-Ala, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, that a freed slave of his bought wine and made a profit in it, so Uthman said to him: Return it, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wine and prohibited its price. Salim said: And Yunus narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, with the like of it. And this hadith, we do not know of any path for it from Uthman except what we have mentioned, though similar words have been narrated from other than Uthman with other than this wording; we shall mention it in its place with its wording, Allah willing."
"2330","2323 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Karima informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salama informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulatha informed us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I hear the crying of a child and I shorten the prayer, fearing that his mother may be distressed."" And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayra and Anas with chains better than this chain, but we mentioned it from Uthman due to the rarity of the hadith of Uthman from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we do not know these words narrated from Uthman except through this way, and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah is layyin (weak) in hadith, while the rest are well known."
"2331","2324 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh al-Marwazi and Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, they said: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath informed us, he said: My father informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn al-Hakam, who is the nephew of Uthman ibn Abi al-As, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He who sends forth three children in Islam before him has shielded himself with a thick shield from the Fire."" And this hadith, we do not recall any path for it from Uthman except this one, nor is this wording preserved from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this way with this chain, even if similar in meaning has been narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through several ways. And Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq is a Kufan, called Abu Shayba; Marwan ibn Muawiya, Muhammad ibn Fudayl, al-Qasim ibn Malik, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, Hafs ibn Ghiyath and others narrated from him, and his hadith is not the hadith of a precise memorizer, though his hadith has been tolerated."
"2332","2325 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Hafs informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn al-Hakam, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned snakes, and he said: Whoever fears their harm is not from us. And this hadith has been narrated from more than one from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever leaves them fearing their retaliation is not from us."" He said: And in this hadith it is ""Whoever fears their harm is not from us,"" so we wrote it due to the difference in wording and because it is not narrated from Uthman except from this place."
"2333","2326 - Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Junayd Abu Shayba informed us, he said: Farwa ibn Abi al-Maghra informed us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Malik informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn al-Hakam, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: When the wind blew fiercely, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: ""O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what is sent in it."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from Uthman except through this way with this chain, though similar words have been narrated from other than Uthman with other than its wording."
"2334","2327 - Bishr ibn Muadh al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Abu Hammam informed us, he said: Said ibn al-Saib al-Taifi informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Iyad, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to place the mosque of Taif where their idol had been. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Uthman ibn Abi al-As with this chain."
"2335","Musnad of Usama ibn Umayr, father of Abu al-Malih (may Allah be pleased with him). Hadith of Abu al-Malih from his father 2328 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awana informed us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Malih, from his father."
"2336","2329 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us, he said: Shuba informed us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Malih, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from ghulul (misappropriated spoils)."" And this hadith, similar words have been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through several ways, narrated by Ibn Umar and Anas, so we mentioned the hadith of Abu Malih from his father to the exclusion of others, for its chain was the best chain among others."
"2337","2330 - Muammal ibn Hisham informed us, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Yazid al-Rishk informed us, from Abu al-Malih (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the skins of predators."""
"2338","2331 - Ahmad ibn al-Sakht narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Yazid al-Rishk informed us, from Abu al-Malih, from his father. Ahmad said: No one else followed him in raising it from his father. As for the hadith of Matar from Abu al-Malih from his father, only Aban narrated it, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Aban except Ishaq ibn Idris."
"2339","2332 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us, he said: Shuba informed us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Malih, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2340","2333 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Muadh ibn Hisham informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Abu al-Malih, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2341","2334 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muadh ibn Hisham informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Abu al-Malih, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: ""We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a rainy day, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered, and it was called out: Prayer in the dwellings."" And this hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through several ways, so we mentioned this path among the paths of what was narrated in this regard."
"2342","2335 - Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutayba informed us, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Fadala, brother of Mubarak ibn Fadala, informed us, he said: Salim Abu Ubayd Allah ibn Salim informed us, from Abu al-Malih, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Fast from wadah to wadah (from crescent to crescent)."" And we do not know it narrated with this wording except through this way, even if similar words are narrated. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Abu Qutayba."
"2343","2336 - Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Wasiti and Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Isa informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Zakariyya al-Ghassani informed us, from Abbad ibn Said, a man from the offspring of Abu al-Malih, from Mubashshir, freed slave of Abu al-Malih, from Abu al-Malih, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer, he said: and I heard him say: ""Lord of Jibril and Mikail and Muhammad, save me from the Fire."" We do not recall it with this wording except with this chain through this way, and Yahya ibn Abi Zakariyya is one against whom there is no harm; people have narrated from him, and Abbad ibn Said and Mubashshir have been narrated from."
"2344","2337 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sulayman al-Dabbas informed us, he said: Abu Said informed us, from Muhajir Abu Habib, from Abu al-Malih, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I enter prayer and I do not know, due to my poor memory, whether I finish on an even number or an odd number? He said: ""When you find that, place your forefinger on your left thigh, for it is from Satan."" We do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this way with this chain. And Abu Said is al-Hasan ibn Dinar, and Muhajir Abu Habib is a Basran, and they are not strong in hadith, but we mentioned this because we did not recall it except through this way."
"2345","2338 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bazi informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman al-Bakrawi informed us, he said: al-Salt ibn Dinar informed us, from Abu al-Malih, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: ""The angels descended on the day of Badr bearing the mark of al-Zubayr, wearing yellow turbans."" And these words have been narrated from other than Usama ibn Umayr, so we mentioned it from Usama ibn Umayr since it is not narrated from Usama except through this path, even though al-Salt is layyin (weak) in hadith, a Basran, and we only included it in the Musnad, though it is not mentioned from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), because it took place with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2346","2339 - Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, he said: al-Minhal ibn Khalifa informed us, from Salama ibn Tammam, from Abu al-Malih, from his father, that a woman threw a stone at a woman and caused a dead fetus to be cast, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) judged in it a ghurra of a slave or a slave-girl. And this hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through several ways, and we do not know it narrated from Abu al-Malih from his father except through this way, and Abu al-Malih has narrated it from Hamal ibn Malik. And the hadith of Abu al-Malih from his father is a hasan chain, because al-Minhal is well known, and Salama ibn Tammam Abu Abd Allah al-Shaqari, so we mentioned it due to the rarity of the hadith of Abu al-Malih from his father. End of the twenty-second juz, and praise be to Allah abundantly, as He deserves."
"2347","Musnad of Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both). Hadith of Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As 2340 - Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib ibn Yahya al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq informed us, he said: Nasr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The just will be on pulpits of light on the Day of Resurrection before the Most Merciful, Mighty and Majestic, on account of their justice in the world."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abd Allah ibn Amr."
"2348","2341 - Nasr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Nasr said: Abd al-Ala informed us, and Abu Musa said: Abd al-Ala informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I said: I shall fast the day and stand the night, then I met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""Are you the one who said: I shall fast the day and stand the night?"" He said: I said: I did say that, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You cannot bear that, so stand and sleep, and fast and break fast; fast three days from every month, for that is like fasting the whole year."" He said: I said: I can bear better than that. He said: ""Fast one day and break fast two days."" I said: I can bear better than that. He said: ""Fast one day and break fast one day, and that is the most just fasting, and it is the fast of Dawud (peace be upon him)."" I said: I can bear better than that. He said: ""There is nothing better than that."""
"2349","2342 - And Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated it to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"2350","2343 - And Khalid ibn Yusuf informed us of it, he said: Abu Awana informed us, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr."
"2351","2344 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Shayban informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Fast and break fast, and sleep and stand; fast three days from every month."" I said: I can bear more than that. He said: ""Fast one day and break fast one day; fast the fast of Dawud."""
"2352","2345 - And Yusuf ibn Musa informed us of it, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, he said: Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I was a striving man, then I married, so my father came to the woman and said to her: How do you find your husband? She said: An excellent man of a man; he does not sleep and does not break fast, so there occurred between me and my father, and he said: I married you to a woman of the Muslims and you did to her what you did? And I did not care what he said, due to the strength I felt, until that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""But I sleep and pray, and fast and break fast, so fast and pray, and sleep and stand; fast three days from every month."" I said: I am stronger than that. He said: ""Then fast the fast of Dawud (peace be upon him): fast one day and break fast one day, and recite the Quran in every month."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am stronger than that. He said: ""Recite it in fifteen."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am stronger than that, and it continued until it reached seven, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every deed has a sharra (fervor), and every sharra has a fatra (lapse), so whoever’s lapse is toward my Sunna has been guided, and whoever’s lapse is toward other than that has perished."" And Abd Allah ibn Amr said when he grew old and weak: That I had accepted the concession of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is more beloved to me than my family and wealth."
"2353","2346 - al-Hasan ibn Arafa narrated to us, he said: Hushaym informed us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman and al-Mughira, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: My father married me to a woman of Quraysh, and when she came to me, I think he said: I did not turn to her, or I did not care for her, due to my worship of fasting and prayer, so Amr ibn al-As came to her and said to her: How did you find your husband? She said: Like the best of men and like the best of husbands of a man; he has not uncovered for us a curtain, nor approached for us a bed, so he turned to me and bit me with his tongue, and said: I married you to a woman of lineage and you did and did, then he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained of me to him. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for me and said to me: ""Do you fast the day?"" I said: Yes. He said: ""And do you stand the night?"" I said: Yes. He said: ""For I fast and break fast, and pray and sleep."" Then he said to me: ""Recite the Quran in a month."" He said: I said: I find myself stronger than that. He said: ""Then recite it in fifteen."" I said: I find myself stronger than that. One of them, either Husayn or Mughira, said: He said: ""Then recite it in every three."" Then he said: ""And fast three days from every month."" I said: I am stronger than that. He said: And he kept with me until he said: ""Fast one day and break fast one day, for that is the best fasting, and it is the fast of Dawud (peace be upon him)."" Hushaym said: Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman said in his hadith: Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every deed has a sharra (fervor) and every sharra has a fatra (lapse), either toward a sunna or toward a bidah (innovation), so whoever’s lapse is toward my Sunna has been guided, and whoever’s lapse is toward other than that"" - and Husayn said: ""has perished"" - ""and I have a deed; when I am fervent I complete it, and when I lapse I recite,"" meaning he would recite."
"2354","2347 - And Muhammad ibn al-Walid informed us of it, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us, he said: Shuba informed us, from Husayn, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of the hadith of Husayn."
"2355","2348 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Yamar ibn Bishr informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Shuba, from Qatada, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2356","2349 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us of it, he said: Dawud informed us, he said: Hammam informed us, from Qatada, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not look at a woman who is not grateful to her husband while she cannot dispense with him."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except by Abd Allah ibn Amr, and we do not know anyone who narrated it marfu from Shuba except Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak."
"2357","2350 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi informed us, he said: Said informed us, from Qatada, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Juwayriya on a Friday while she was fasting, and said to her: ""Did you fast yesterday?"" She said: No. He said: ""Will you fast tomorrow?"" She said: No. He said: ""Then break your fast."" And this hadith, Said differed in it with Shuba: Shuba said: Qatada narrated to us from Abu Ayyub from Juwayriya, while Said said: As for what I memorized, I and Matar, it is from Qatada from Ibn al-Musayyib from Abd Allah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2358","2351 - Muhammad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jahdam informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for anyone to say: I am better than Yahya ibn Zakariyya; he did not intend a sin - I think he said - nor did he do it."
"2359","2352 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Numayr informed us, he said: Uthman ibn Hakim informed us, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and while we were with him he said: ""A cursed man will surely enter upon you,"" and I had left Amr ibn al-As putting on his clothes to catch up with me, and I kept looking anxiously until al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As entered. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abd Allah ibn Amr with this chain."
"2360","2353 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Affan informed us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad informed us, he said: Uthman ibn Hakim informed us, he said: I heard Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf say: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not come until you couple in the roads like the coupling of donkeys."""
"2361","2354 - And al-Fahm ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us of it, he said: Abd Allah ibn Numayr informed us, he said: Uthman ibn Hakim informed us, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, with the like of it, though he did not raise it except that he said: ""The Hour will not come until people couple in the roads like the coupling of donkeys."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated through a sound way except from Abd Allah ibn Amr with this chain."
"2362","2355 - al-Qasim ibn Bishr ibn Maruf narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi informed us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad informed us, from Musa ibn Jubayr, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Leave the Abyssinians as long as they leave you, for none shall extract the treasure of the Kaba except Dhu al-Suwayqatayn of the Abyssinians."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abd Allah ibn Amr with this chain, and we do not know anyone who said from Abu Umama from Abd Allah ibn Amr except al-Qasim ibn Bishr from Abu Amir, while others said from Abu Umama from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2363","2356 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama and Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, with the wording of Yusuf, they said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: ""The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so it was called out: Prayer in congregation, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed twice in one prostration, then stood and bowed twice in one prostration - meaning he prostrated once in every two rakas - then the sun cleared."" Aisha said: I never prostrated a prostration nor bowed a bowing longer than it."
"2364","2357 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir informed us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man will commit ilhad (deviation) in Makka called Abd Allah; upon him is half the punishment of the worlds."" And this hadith has been differed upon from al-Awzai: Muhammad ibn Kathir said from al-Awzai from Yahya from Abu Salama from Abd Allah ibn Amr, and he was not followed in this chain, while others said from al-Awzai from Muhammad, a man of the family of al-Mughira ibn Shuba, from al-Mughira ibn Shuba from Uthman ibn Affan."
"2365","2358 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Missisi informed us, he said: al-Awzai informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Do not be like so-and-so; he used to stand the night then abandoned standing the night. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except by Abd Allah ibn Amr, nor do we know it narrated from Yahya except by al-Awzai."
"2366","2359 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Shayban informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salama, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Recite the Quran in a month."
"2367","2360 - Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us, he said: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman and Mirdas, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying the two rakas of Fajr after the Fajr prayer had been established, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The morning four?"" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abd Allah ibn Amr except through this way, nor do we know it narrated from Muhammad ibn Amr except by al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman."
"2368","2361 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid informed us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu Yahya, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing."" He said: So I came to him and found him praying sitting, and he said: ""What is with you, O Abd Allah ibn Amr?"" I said: You narrated to us that the prayer of a man sitting is half the prayer, yet you pray sitting? He said: ""Yes, but I am not like any one of you."""
"2369","2362 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir informed us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu Yahya, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: We returned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Makka to Madina, until when we were on the road we came upon people who had performed wudu while their feet were white, gleaming, untouched by water, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Perform wudu fully; woe to the heels from the Fire."""
"2370","2363 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik informed us of it, he said: Abu Awana informed us, from Abu Bishr, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""Woe to the heels from the Fire."""
"2371","2364 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Amr ibn Aws, that he heard Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: The most beloved fasting to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is the fasting of Dawud: he would fast one day and break fast one day, and the most beloved prayer to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is the prayer of Dawud: he would sleep half the night, stand a third of it, and sleep a sixth of it. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording from Abd Allah ibn Amr except with this chain."
"2372","2365 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: We prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night; those who left left, and those who stayed behind stayed, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came before the people called out for the Isha prayer, and said: ""Rejoice, rejoice; this is your Lord, Blessed and Exalted, has opened a door of the doors of heaven, boasting of you to the angels, saying: Look at My servants; they have fulfilled an obligation and are awaiting another."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with him), nor do we know a path for it from Abd Allah ibn Amr except this path."
"2373","2366 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid informed us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2374","2367 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar informed us of it, he said: Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr informed us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman informed us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""Be upright, and you will not encompass; and know that the best of your deeds is prayer, and none preserves wudu except a believer."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abd Allah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this way with this chain."
"2375","2368 - Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn Khalaf narrated to us, they said: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman informed us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The transgressing party shall kill Ammar."""
"2376","2369 - Abbad ibn Yaqub al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Quddus informed us, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2377","2370 - And Abbad ibn Yaqub informed us, he said: Abu Yahya al-Taymi informed us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""It is imminent that Allah shall fill your hands with the non-Arabs, then make them lions who do not flee; they shall fight your fighters and consume your fay (spoils)."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abd Allah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this way with this chain."
"2378","2371 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra informed us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Amr informed us, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The maintainer of ties is not the requiter, but the maintainer is the one who, when his kinship is cut, joins it."""
"2379","2372 - And Ahmad ibn Abda informed us of it, he said: Umar ibn Ali informed us, he said: Fitr informed us, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The maintainer is not the requiter, but the maintainer is the one who, when his kinship is cut, joins it."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abd Allah ibn Amr except through this way with this chain."
"2380","2373 - Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra informed us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Amr informed us, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever kills a person of the dhimma (protected people) shall not smell the fragrance of Paradise, though its scent is found from a distance of forty years."""
"2381","2374 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah al-Rabai informed us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Amr informed us, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""When you see my umma fearing the wrongdoer to say: You are a wrongdoer, then they have been forsaken."""
"2382","2375 - And Yusuf ibn Musa informed us of it, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi informed us, from Ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""When you see my umma fearing the wrongdoer to say: You are a wrongdoer, then they have been forsaken."" And this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Amr from Abu al-Zubayr is the correct one in my view."
"2383","2376 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra al-Dawsi informed us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Amr informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""Indeed, among my umma there shall be khaf (sinking), maskh (transformation), and qadhf (pelting)."" And we do not know that Abu al-Zubayr narrated marfu from Abd Allah ibn Amr except these two hadiths."
"2384","2377 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2385","2378 - And Ali ibn Said al-Masruqi informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever drinks wine and puts it in his belly, his prayer shall not be accepted for seven; if he dies in it he dies a disbeliever, and if it removes his reason from any of the obligations, his prayer shall not be accepted for forty days; if he dies in it he dies a disbeliever."""
"2386","2379 - And Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan informed us, he said: My father informed us, he said: Fitr ibn Khalifa informed us, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"2387","2380 - And Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi informed us, he said: My father informed us, he said: Fitr ibn Khalifa informed us, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is intoxicated by wine, his prayer shall not be accepted for forty days; if he dies in it he dies like a worshipper of idols."""
"2388","2381 - al-Abbas ibn Jafar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur informed us, he said: Israil informed us, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: ""A man passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing two red garments, and he greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but he did not return the greeting upon him."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abd Allah ibn Amr, nor do we know a path for it except this path, nor do we know it narrated from Israil except by Ishaq ibn Mansur."
"2389","2382 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn Muhammad informed us, he said: Fitr ibn Khalifa informed us, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The drinker of wine is like a worshipper of idols."" And Thabit ibn Muhammad did not place anyone between Fitr and Mujahid."
"2390","2383 - Ahmad ibn Yazdad al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar al-Fuqaymi informed us, he said: al-Amash informed us, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever kills a muahad (one under covenant) shall not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and whoever claims (lineage) to other than his father - I think he said - shall not smell the fragrance of Paradise, though its scent is found from a distance of forty years."""
"2391","2384 - Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf informed us, from Sharik, he said: Muslim informed us, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: ""We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); among us was one fasting and among us one breaking fast, and the fasting did not reproach the breaking, nor the breaking the fasting."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abd Allah ibn Amr except through this way. And Muslim from whom Sharik narrated this is Muslim Abu Abd Allah al-Awar; Shuba, al-Thawri, Israil and others narrated from him."
"2392","2385 - al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban al-Anazi informed us, he said: Mindal ibn Ali informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu once each. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abd Allah ibn Amr except by Mujahid, nor from Mujahid except by Ibn Abi Najih."
"2393","2386 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, they said: Wahb ibn Jarir informed us, he said: Shuba informed us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2394","2387 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talha informed us, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."""
"2395","2388 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutayba informed us, he said: Bashir Abu Ismail informed us, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Jibril kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Mujahid except by Bashir. And they differed from Mujahid in this hadith: Zubayd al-Ayami said from Mujahid from Aisha from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq said from Mujahid from Abu Hurayra from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while Bashir said from Mujahid from Abd Allah ibn Amr."
"2396","2389 - Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: Yaman ibn al-Mughira informed us, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs wudu excellently, then prays four rakas in which he does not err, is forgiven."""
"2397","2390 - Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalid informed us, he said: Ibn Lahia informed us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw upon a man a garment dyed with safflower, and said: ""What is this?"" So Abd Allah went and burned it with fire, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""What did you do with your garment?"" He said: I burned it. He said: ""Why did you not clothe someone with it?"""
"2398","2391 - Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Salt informed us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Abd Allah ibn Amr."
"2399","2392 - And Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Ubayda al-Usfuri informed us of it, he said: Fudayl ibn Abd al-Wahhab informed us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: ""That which does not make death beloved to me: al-Sadiqa (the truthful); they said: And what is al-Sadiqa? He said: A sahifa (script) I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" And the meaning of this hadith is that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him to write from him."
"2400","2393 - Uqba ibn Mukram and Abu Burayd al-Jarmi narrated to us, they said: Ibn Abi Adi informed us, he said: Shuba informed us, from Yala ibn Ata, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The passing of the whole world is lighter upon Allah, Blessed and Exalted, than the blood of a Muslim shed without right - or he said - killed without right."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it marfu from Shuba except Ibn Abi Adi."
